"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
21043,"(21043) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible to bear witness to a slanderer, and he repented. What is between him and God?"
21044,"(21044) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I repented him that he should lie to himself."
21045,"(21045) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: His repentance is that he should stand like he did and be lied to. Himself"
21046,"(21046) Hafs and Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit and Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuraih, said: The one who manages it should not be sold."
21047,"(21047) Abu Khaled and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: The one who manages it does not sell her to her master, nor marry her to her, nor give her and her children to her status."
21048,"(21048) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Othman bin Hakim, who said: I asked Salim: Is it permissible for me to sell it? He said: No, I said: Should I command her? He said: No."
21049,"(21049) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The one who was freed from the back of his house, except that he It cannot be sold or given away. If his master dies, he is freed."
21050,"(21050) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked selling a emancipator without delay, unless he was His companion is extremely poor."
21051,"(21051) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; He disliked selling a emancipated person off his back, except on his own behalf."
21052,"(21052) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ayyub, and Isham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The manager is not sold except by himself."
21053,"(21053) Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He does not sell it unless he needs its price."
21054,"(21054) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kail, on the authority of Ata’, and Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sold a property that turned away. (Bukhari 2141. An-Nasa’i 6250)"
21055,"(21055) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, that a man managed a boy and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold him to him. He handed over to Ibn al-Nahham a Coptic boy who died in the first year of Ibn al-Zubayr’s rule. (Bukhari 2231, Muslim 1289)"
21056,"(21056) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar disliked selling the manager."
21057,"(21057) Ismail bin Ibrahim, who is Ibn Aliyah, narrated to us on the authority of Yahya bin Yazid al-Na’i, who said: I asked Anas bin Malik about a man who gave gifts to his debtor, and he said: If he gave gifts to him before that, then there is no problem, but if not. If it is given to him before that, it will not be good."
21058,"(21058) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas said: If you lend a loan, do not You may guide someone like a sheep, or ride an animal."
21059,"(21059) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Kulthum ibn Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: He said Ubayy: When you lent a loan, then the person who provided the loan came carrying it and had a gift, took his loan from him, and returned it to him. This is your gift"
21060,"(21060) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: If a man owes a debtor to a man So he brought it to him so that he would delay it, so let him count it as part of his religion."
21061,"(21061) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If this had happened between them before The religion calls him and the other calls him and he is rewarded, so there is no harm in that, and do not count it as part of his religion."
21062,"(21062) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If they were talking to one another before That's okay."
21063,"(21063) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Ubayy had a debt on Umar and he paid it back. He brought it to him and returned it, so Omar said: Usury is only imposed on whoever wants to keep it and forget it."
21064,"(21064) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Abi Anisa, that Ali was asked about A man lends a loan to another man and gives him a gift. He said: That is usury."
21065,"(21065) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He is the one who narrates it."
21066,"(21066) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: It was It is disliked for a man to eat from another man’s house when he has a debt, unless he counts it as part of his debt."
21067,"(21067) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, and Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Amer, who said: If There is a debt on the man, so do not show him hospitality."
21068,"(21068) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It was mentioned to Ibn Masoud that a man lent A man bought dirhams and stipulated the back of his horse. He said: Whatever he buys from the back of his horse is usury."
21069,"(21069) Shihab bin Muhammad Al-Amiri told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I said to him: If I have A man asked me to borrow an animal from him, or ask him for a favor. He said: There is no problem."
21070,"(21070) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to say: decree and praise."
21071,"(21071) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Do not buy anything from someone who is under duress."
21072,"(21072) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who said: There was a shareholder who did not permit the sale of Pressure"
21073,"(21073) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Maqil, who said: A distressed person is sold for usury."
21074,"(21074) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel and Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: I said to Ibrahim: The man He is tortured, should I buy from him? He said: No."
21075,"(21075) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not buy anything from someone under pressure."
21076,"(21076) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Salem, who said: It is forbidden to sell to someone who is forced to do so."
21077,"(21077) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: They used to hate every loan that brought benefit."
21078,"(21078) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every loan that brings in a benefit is usury."
21079,"(21079) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they disavowed every loan that brought benefit."
21080,"(21080) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: A man lent another man five hundred dirhams. He stipulated that he should pay the back of his horse, and Ibn Masoud said: Whatever he stipulates of the back of his horse is usury."
21081,"(21081) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, that he hated every loan that was repaid. Beneficial"
21082,"(21082) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that he disliked fresh dates with dates, example for example. He said: Dates are swollen, and dates are dried."
21083,"(21083) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He disliked buying fresh dates for dry dates."
21084,"(21084) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Wet things cannot be bought with dry ones."
21085,"(21085) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade selling fruit for a measure of dates, and selling grapes for a measure of raisins, and selling crops. With wheat as a measure.
(Muslim 1171. Abu Dawud 3354)"
21086,"(21086) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah bin Qadamah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He disliked dates with dates, and said: It is the smaller of the two in a measure or in a qafiz."
21087,"(21087) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid, on the authority of Zaid Abi Ayyash, who said: I asked Saad about salt with corn, what he thought of it, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about rutab with dates, and he said: Does it decrease when it dries? They said: Yes, he thought about it. (Tirmidhi 1225. Ibn Majah 2264)"
21088,"(21088) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that he disliked mixing wet dates with dry ones, example for example."
21089,"(21089) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim and others, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Who He emancipated a portion of his property, and he owned all of it, or part of it, so he emancipated all of it."
21090,"(21090) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, about a man who said to his female servant: Your relief. Free, he said: She is free, and if any of her is freed, then she is free."
21091,"(21091) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid bin Salamah, who said: A man came to Omar and he knew him, and he said: I I freed a third of my slave, and Omar said: He is completely free, he has no partner."
21092,"(21092) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: If he frees part of it, then all of it is free."
21093,"(21093) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who freed a third of his slaves. He said: He will strive for him in Two-thirds, and there is no guarantee for the remainder of it."
21094,"(21094) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, that a man freed a third of his servants, Then it was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: He is free, he has no partner. (Abu Dawud 3929. Ahmad 5/75)"
21095,"(21095) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the arbitrator, about a man, who said to his servant: Half of you is free. He said: If As they say: The guarantee is a right, so it is freed, and it was the arbiter’s opinion that he should free him. He said: I asked Hammad and he said: He should be freed. Half of it, and he sa'y with the remaining half."
21096,"(21096) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ali said: A man may free as many of his servants as he wishes."
21097,"(21097) Abdid bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he frees a few or many of his servants, So he is freed, and if he divorces his wife by a finger, or more than that, then he is divorced."
21098,"(21098) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Sunnah has passed that it is permissible for women to be witnesses. When no one else is aware of women’s births and their defects, and it is permissible for the midwife alone to bear witness regarding the istihlaal, And two women besides that. (Abdul Razzaq 15427)"
21099,"(21099) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, regarding a matter in which the testimony of men is not permissible: Four women. The arbitrator said: Two women are sufficient."
21100,"(21100) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is permissible for women to bear witness to the istilal."
21101,"(21101) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amer, who said: Among the testimonies are testimonies in which only Testimonies of women."
21102,"(21102) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi said: It is permissible for one woman to be a witness in matters that are not privy to men."
21103,"(21103) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is not permissible to have less than four witnesses. Women in matters in which it is not permissible for men to witness."
21104,"(21104) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Shurayh, that he approved the testimony of Qibla."
21105,"(21105) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali, that he permitted Shahadī He met him."
21106,"(21106) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, and Abu Hanifi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: It is permissible for a witness to meet him. One, and one of them said: Even if she is Jewish."
21107,"(21107) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Among the witnesses is a witness, in which only a witness is permissible. A woman"
21108,"(21108) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of a group of witnesses who disagreed, so one of them testified against him. Twenty and the other is on ten. He said: It is taken as ten."
21109,"(21109) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: the same."
21110,"(21110) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Omar bin Abdullah bin Wathili, he said: Two witnesses witnessed. According to one of them, he said it was more and the other was less, so he accepted their testimony as saying what was less."
21111,"(21111) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Abdullah bin Malih Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Omar bin Abdullah bin Wathil, He said: He testified with Sharih, one of them testified for a thousand and the other for five hundred, so Shurayh allowed their testimony to be five. A hundred"
21112,"(21112) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He has two oxen."
21113,"(21113) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: All of your affairs will come back unless a man says to another man: I will sell to you what so-and-so and so-and-so owes for such-and-such, and if he sells it he will not return it."
21114,"(21114) Yahya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyy, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, he said: He will not return. In the transfer to its owner until he becomes bankrupt, or dies, and does not leave repayment, for a man is sometimes easy and sometimes difficult."
21115,"(21115) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bai, on the authority of Khalid bin Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Uthman, about the following: He returns, but he does not have the money of a Muslim who has just passed away."
21116,"(21116) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he deceives He was full, then he went bankrupt after that, so it is permissible for him."
21117,"(21117) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khattab al-Asfari, who said: A man referred me to a Jew who had turned me around, so I asked al-Sha’abi. He said: Go back to the beginning."
21118,"(21118) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Shurayh; Concerning a man, a man turns his back and he turns. He said: He returns to the first time."
21119,"(21119) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, something similar."
21120,"(21120) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, that he disliked to say: I bought from you what so-and-so owed, and he said: This is deception."
21121,"(21121) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not consider the person in charge to be innocent unless he was acquitted, If He acquits him, then he is acquitted."
21122,"(21122) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Al-Thaqafi, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote, Women give to their husbands willingly and out of fear. Whenever a woman gives her husband something and she wants it, You squeeze him, so she has more right to him."
21123,"(21123) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Amir, who said: The woman should not return to her husband, nor The man returns to his dignity."
21124,"(21124) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a man and a woman, neither of them has the right to take back what he gave to its owner."
21125,"(21125) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Omar bin Abd al-Aziz regarding the husband. And the woman does not have the right to take back what he gave to its owner."
21126,"(21126) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A woman came to quarrel with her husband. A comment about something she gave him. Then the man said: Has not God Almighty said: (And if he pleases you for any of it, So eat him in good health. Shurayh said: If her soul was happy with it, she would not quarrel with you."
21127,"(21127) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: Two just witnesses. She left him without any hatred or disgrace."
21128,"(21128) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father Tawus, who said: If the woman gives birth To her husband, then she returned and he would be returned to her."
21129,"(21129) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a woman gives her husband and Having a good soul is permissible, and Mansour said: I do not like it."
21130,"(21130) Ibn Abi Za’idah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amir, who said: She will be entitled to what he gave her. He married her off, and he is not allowed to take back what she gave him."
21131,"(21131) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man mortgages the land, he does not have the right to work it. There is something in it, so if he does anything in it, it will be credited to the owner of the land from what he mortgaged it, like the reward for something like it."
21132,"(21132) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, about a man who mortgaged land to his wife for her friends. So she ate some of the expensive food, and he said: Do not be held accountable for it."
21133,"(21133) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who mortgaged a female slave who had a son and she breastfed for him. He said: It will be calculated for him the reward of a female slave for what she breastfed."
21134,"(21134) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he benefits from something mortgaged, He told him as much as that."
21135,"(21135) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a man who took a mortgage of a house, or A boy, so he took advantage of him and said: The ransom is from the mortgage."
21136,"(21136) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If he acknowledges a debt to an heir, it is permissible."
21137,"(21137) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Amir Al-Ahwal, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about it and he said: I will carry it for you, but I will not carry it. about him"
21138,"(21138) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, And on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: If he confesses during an illness For an heir who is in debt, it is not permissible except with evidence, and if it is confirmed that there is no heir, then it is permissible."
21139,"(21139) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Udhain. Concerning a man who acknowledges a debt to an heir, he said: It is not permissible."
21140,"(21140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is not permissible to confess to the sick."
21141,"(21141) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who acknowledged a debt to an heir, he said: It is permissible."
21142,"(21142) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sharih, that It was permissible for a man to confess a debt to someone other than an heir upon his death, and he would not allow it to be owed to an heir except with clear evidence."
21143,"(21143) Omar bin Ayyub al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: If a man acknowledges a debt during his illness So I think that it is permissible for him, because if he acknowledges it and it is true, it is permissible and more true than what will be at the time of his death."
21144,"(21144) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If you sell food for a specified period and the deadline has come, do not take the food. He said: Jabir bin Zaid Abu Al-Sha’tha’i said: If your dinar is available, take with it whatever you want."
21145,"(21145) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, who said: I said to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: Did you sell dates to a man and take dates from the price? He said: Do not take food that has not been measured and weighed."
21146,"(21146) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amer, who said: If you sell food for a specified period of time and it is permissible for your money to be taken, then take it. Whatever you want of the offerings, do not take any food except your food with your own eyes."
21147,"(21147) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, regarding a man A man sold a sheep for a set period of time, and when the deadline came, he wanted to take the sheep and settle his mind."
21148,"(21148) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith and Hammad that they were reluctant for a man to sell food. A Kurr for forty nis, then he buys food from him, the same without the forty."
21149,"(21149) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Ibn Abbas said: If you sell A sale of what is measured and weighed for a specific period. Your term is permissible, so do not take them, but take what is different from them."
21150,"(21150) Hammad bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Suleiman bin Yesar, they said: Whoever sells food for gold for a specified period and then the specified period is due, then he should not take dates with it."
21151,"(21151) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not take a measure."
21152,"(21152) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: I asked Tawoos about a man who sold another man’s property for a specified period. The term: Should I take land in place of my money? He said: No."
21153,"(21153) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no harm in someone taking his place."
21154,"(21154) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Concerning a man who sells food for a period of time and it is permissible, but he does not have any dirhams. He said: Take whatever you want."
21155,"(21155) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Take whatever you want."
21156,"(21156) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: This is food for food."
21157,"(21157) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Muhammad was asked about a man who sells goods for a term, then the term is due. Should he take possessions? He said: The man used to go to his debtor and take it from him, so it was said to him: Should I sell food and take the food? He said: I do not say anything about it."
21158,"(21158) Muhammad ibn Mus’ab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Omar ibn Abd ruled Al-Aziz, regarding the deceased’s debt regarding food, said: He does not take food."
21159,"(21159) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who buys a house and builds it, then an intercessor comes. He said: He takes it for its construction, or for its value. He said: Hammad: Its builders will uproot it and take it."
21160,"(21160) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, that a man bought a house and built it, then a man came and claimed it. So he decreed that the pillar should be straightened and the builder should be straightened. If he wanted, the builder would take it for his value, even if he refused to hand over the hill. At its value."
21161,(21161) Waki’ said: Sufyan said: Its builders will be uprooted.
21162,"(21162) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ikrimah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, about a man who married a woman who owned a house. Then the intercessor of the house asked for the house. He said: They took it with a truth like a mirror. He said: And Ibn Shubrumah said: I do not see that, but The intercessor took it for the value."
21163,"(21163) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no pre-emption in Sadaq."
21164,"(21164) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I narrated on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There is no intercessor in Sadaq."
21165,"(21165) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hassan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla; Concerning a man who marries the house, he said: The intercessor takes it for the value of the house."
21166,"(21166) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you owe a debt to a man and you do not know where he is. And where is his heir? So give it in charity on his behalf, and if he comes, give him good."
21167,"(21167) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Hanash, on the authority of Ibn Umar, about a man who died while in debt. He did not know the owner of the debt, so he ordered that the debt be given in charity on his behalf."
21168,"(21168) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man dies owing a debt, he does not know where. His heir, let him give it to him in the way of God, and if he is a Muslim and does not know where his heir is, let him give it in charity on his behalf."
21169,"(21169) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Amir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah bought a female slave for seven hundred dirhams. Then her companion was absent, so he recognized her for a year, or he said: a year, then he went out to the mosque, and gave alms, and said: Oh God, let him have it. He came to me and to me, then he said: Thus and do with the caught animal or with the lost animal."
21170,"(21170) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, who said: I bought a female slave for five shares. I found with her fifteen dinars, so I brought them to Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid bin al-Walid, and he said: This is yours."
21171,"(21171) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who bought captives from the spoils. He found some silver with her and said: Return it."
21172,"(21172) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, that a man bought a mother on the Day of Qadisiyah for spoils, and she came to him. With some jewelry that he had with her, he came to Saad bin Abi Waqqas and told him, and he said: Put it among the spoils of the Muslims."
21173,"(21173) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri, Jisr Anizah, he said: I said to Maqil Ibn Yasar: The man among us wants to emancipate the emancipated person. He said: If you buy a emancipated person that you want to emancipate, do not stipulate that his family Emancipation, for it is a piece of slavery, but buy it silently. If you wish, you may keep it, and if you wish, you may free it."
21174,"(21174) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: I narrated this hadith to Ayyub, and he said: It is not complete."
21175,"(21175) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he used to say about a man who had a neck on him. So he bought it and stipulated that he emancipate it. He said: He thought so, and said: It is not completely."
21176,"(21176) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of al-Shu’bi, they said: If he bought her and stipulated that she be freed, they would not have seen her intact."
21177,"(21177) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the case of a man who has an obligatory slave, so he buys it: He does not stipulate that he buys it for emancipation."
21178,"(21178) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Harun bin Musa, he said: Ali bin Zayed informed me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he was asked about a man who buys a female slave and makes her master stipulate that she should be freed. He said: The reward goes to her master who He stipulated"
21179,"(21179) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding people who share in justice. He said: There is no harm in They sell to each other before they divide."
21180,"(21180) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked him about some personal belongings. Two men, one of whom was selling his share before dividing it with him. He said: There is no problem with it."
21181,"(21181) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The two partners leave."
21182,"(21182) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not see any harm in a man selling Heirlooms before dividing them."
21183,"(21183) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He hated selling what he could divide. Until it is divided, if it is something that cannot be divided, then there is no problem with it."
21184,"(21184) Abd al-Wahhab al-Khafaf told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, that He saw no harm in a partner selling from his partner unless he divided it with him except for the measure and weight."
21185,"(21185) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, that Ibn Masoud bought land as a tax."
21186,"(21186) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, with a similar matter."
21187,"(21187) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: Do not buy anything from the land of Al-Sawad except From the people of Banqia, the people of Al-Hira, and the people of Al-Alessa."
21188,"(21188) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they were unwilling to buy from the Sultan some land. The penalty"
21189,"(21189) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar wrote: You do not have the right to buy from the property of the people of Dhimma, nor anything from their country."
21190,"(21190) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Raja’ bin Abi Salama, who said: Na’im bin Salama informed me that Omar bin Abd Al-Aziz gave a man land on which he would pay tribute."
21191,"(21191) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Rajaa told me, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: It was They have land from which they pay tribute."
21192,"(21192) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Sama’i, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, who said: I asked about buying land. The tax with its water, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade that you make small children on your necks after he rescued you. God is from him"
21193,"(21193) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man asked him about purchasing The land of the tax, or something similar to its meaning, and he said: You take out the young ones from your neck and put them on your neck."
21194,"(21194) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Miskin, who said: A sheikh narrated to me that he heard Ibn al-Zubayr detesting the purchase of The land of the tribute."
21195,"(21195) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Muhammad ibn Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, Muhammad said: Ibn Bishr: On the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Sufyan al-Uqaili, that Omar said: Do not buy anything from the slaves of non-Muslims. For they are the people of a tax, one of them selling to another, or of their land. (Abdul Razzaq 19290)"
21196,"(21196) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ali, that it was It is disliked to buy anything from the land of kharaj and say: “Muslim tax is due on it.”"
21197,"(21197) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he disliked buying The land of blackness."
21198,"(21198) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Hazim, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I asked him Concerning the purchase of Kharaj land, he said: Do not sell it, nor buy it."
21199,"(21199) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he was reluctant to buy the land of al-Jiziya."
21200,"(21200) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: Shuraih used to swear on the unseen pest. On his knowledge, and on the outward appearance of all."
21201,"(21201) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salem, that Ibn Umar sold a boy for eight hundred Dirhams, and the buyer found a defect in it, so he disputed it with Uthman. He said: Then Uthman asked him, and he said: I sold it for sale, so he said: I swear to him: I have sold it and there is nothing wrong with it, you know."
21202,"(21202) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who buys luggage or goods and finds a defect in them. He said: The buyer seeks clear evidence, because he was at The seller, if there is one. Otherwise, the seller must swear on his knowledge. Amr bin Dinar said: He must swear on his knowledge."
21203,"(21203) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, about a man who bought a female slave who was afflicted with leprosy, but he did not have it. Witnesses said: The seller swears by God: He did not sell it with leprosy on it."
21204,"(21204) Waki’ told us, he said: Omar bin Dhar told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman used to ask a man to swear He defended him from a right he had known to him, and Al-Sha’bi said in Al-Yamin Al-Mursalali: His sin and righteousness depend on what he deliberately did."
21205,"(21205) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ata’ Al-Madini, on the authority of his father, that a man A man sold goods, and the buyer claimed a defect, so he disputed with him to Othman bin Affan, and the buyer said: I swear to God: What You sold me a defect. The seller said: I swear to God: I sold you and I do not know of a defect. He said: Then Uthman said: The man did justice to you."
21206,"(21206) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Al-Zubayr bin Junada told me, he said: I asked Salim about a white land. I bought it from someone who owns its property so that I can build it. He said: There is no problem. He said: So I said: He will pay the tax on its behalf. He said: No. It is bad. I said: I acknowledge the minor ones. He said: That is only in the heads of men."
21207,"(21207) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said to me: Beware of you. And selling private goods is a luxury item, and entertainment is not permissible for a Muslim."
21208,"(21208) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, who said: It was said: Translation is amazing."
21209,"(21209) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Do not receive or celebrate. (Tirmidhi 1268 and Ahmad 1/256)"
21210,"(21210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If one of you sells wheat or sheep, he should not celebrate it.
(Ahmad 2/481, Ibn Majah 2241)"
21211,"(21211) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He narrated to us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is the truthful and trustworthy, said: Selling private goods is picturesque, and it is not permissible to sell picturesque things to a Muslim."
21212,"(21212) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not permissible to emancipate a boy, nor Sell it or buy it."
21213,"(21213) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: It is not permissible to buy a boy, nor sell him, except with permission. His guardian"
21214,"(21214) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: Is it permissible to buy and sell it? He said: If it is permissible to buy and sell it, then freeing him is permissible."
21215,"(21215) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible to buy or sell a boy."
21216,"(21216) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, greeted a caller, and he called until he reached the two: It is not permissible for an adversary to bear witness, nor for those who suspect, and the oath is upon the one who claims. Aliyah (Abu Dawud 3961 and Abd al-Razzaq 15365)"
21217,"(21217) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Muammar Al-Basri, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa, the oath is on the one who denies it."
21218,"(21218) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`iya, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The year has passed. The oath is on the defendant."
21219,"(21219) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Hassan Abi Al-Ashras, on the authority of Shurayh that a man came to him and said: This is what he sold to me, a slave girl with a twisted neck. Shurayh said: I made it clear to you that he sold you out of harm’s way, otherwise he will swear to God: He did not sell you a disease."
21220,"(21220) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, and Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that he said to a man: Swear that you did not sell him a disease."
21221,"(21221) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He ruled on the oath upon the defendant. (Bukhari 2514, Muslim 1336)"
21222,"(21222) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, pronounced the oath on the wanted person. (Bayhaqi 10. Daraqutni 219)"
21223,"(21223) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever swears an oath and fulfills it An immoral person to seize the wealth of a Muslim man with it. He met God while he was angry with him. Al-Ash’ath said: By God, it was revealed: It was. There was a land between me and a Jewish man, but he denied me, so I presented it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Do you have a clear proof? So I said: No, so he said to the Jew: Swear, so I said: Then he will swear and take my money, so God revealed: {Indeed, those who buy For the covenant of God and their oaths, a small price. (Bukhari 2416. Muslim 221)"
21224,"(21224) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, he said: I asked Abu Qalabi about the teacher who teaches. And he takes a reward, but he sees no harm in it."
21225,"(21225) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: He did not see any harm in The teacher teaches, but does not share. If he is given something, he takes it."
21226,"(21226) Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Othman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: The teacher does not stipulate, And if he is given something, let him accept it."
21227,"(21227) Abu Saad Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: He did not see any harm in The teacher takes what he was given without any conditions."
21228,"(21228) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa al-Dimashqi, on the authority of al-Wadhin ibn Ata`, who said: There were three people in Medina. Teachers teaching boys, so Omar ibn al-Khattab used to provide each of them with fifteen times a month."
21229,"(21229) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hated for the teacher to participate in teaching. The Qur’an."
21230,"(21230) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar ibn Musa, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he disliked for the teacher to associate with him."
21231,"(21231) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in taking a reward from someone who has written it, and he hates the condition."
21232,"(21232) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: He hated to teach. On one condition."
21233,"(21233) Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: His people told us about the ruling, he said: I did not know that anyone hated it. Meaning: the teacher’s reward."
21234,"(21234) Zaid told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said: I hope that God will reward him, He disciplines them and teaches them."
21235,"(21235) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Aidh al-Tai, on the authority of Amer, he said: The teacher does not share If something is offered to him, let him accept it."
21236,"(21236) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mahdi bin Maymun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There was a teacher in Medina. He had some of those big sons. He said: They knew his rights regarding Nowruz and the festival."
21237,"(21237) Waki’ and Hamid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Al Aswad Ibn Tha'labah, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn al-Samit, said: I taught some people from the people of Saffaya the Book and the Qur’an, and a man referred to me. One of them was a bow, so I said: It is not money. Shoot from it in the way of God. I will come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we asked him, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, a man gave me a bow from one of those to whom I used to teach the Scripture and the Qur’an. And it is not money, so throw it away for the sake of God. He said: If you would like to be surrounded by a ring of fire, then accept it.
(Abu Dawud 3409. Ahmad 5/315)"
21238,"(21238) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: It is forbidden to bribe a teacher, for The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated him and saw him severely."
21239,"(21239) Muhammad bin Maysar Abu Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father: that Ubayy bin Ka’b used to teach A blind man, and when he came to him in the morning, he would say: I found it within myself about that, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If something gives you pleasure, then there is no good in it, and if it is his food and the food of his family, then there is no harm in it.
(Ibn Majah 2158, Bayhaqi 126)"
21240,"(21240) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate that They take a reward from the servants in the book."
21241,"(21241) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If you convert to Islam over food, then do not You can take other food in its place, and if you want to take its place with fodder, then take it if you wish."
21242,"(21242) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, that a man converted to Islam over something. He did not find it, so he asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: Take some food, take some sheep."
21243,"(21243) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you embrace Islam safely, there is no harm in taking your capital casually."
21244,"(21244) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: If you convert to Islam in something, do not sell it. Until you take possession of it, and do not spend it in any other way."
21245,"(21245) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: There is no harm in greeting, but do not turn away. Change it, and do not sell it until you have received it."
21246,"(21246) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you embrace Islam in something, do not take except what you have surrendered to. Do not neglect one thing and then transform it into another thing."
21247,"(21247) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awanyah, on the authority of Dawud bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Muslims converted to Islam, so whoever converts to wheat shall not take barley, and whoever converts to barley shall not take He takes wheat in a specified amount for a specified period."
21248,"(21248) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Do not spend your peace in anything until Take hold of it"
21249,"(21249) Ibn Uyaynah and Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the two sellers disagree, then the word is what the seller and the buyer said. By choice.
(Tirmidhi 3370 and Abu Dawud 3505)"
21250,"(21250) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the two sellers disagree and there is no agreement between them It is clear, and the thing sold is in fact, so the statement is the seller’s statement, or they are reluctant to sell, even if the thing sold has already been sold. The statement is the buyer’s statement, and the evidence is on the seller."
21251,"(21251) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to say about If the two sellers disagree and the seller stands in the same manner, he will ask them for the clear evidence. If one of them upholds the clear evidence, he will be given With your proof, and if they do not have proof, they will swear an oath to them, and if they bring them all, the sale will be returned, even if they do not swear an oath. Return the sale, and if one of them swears and the other refuses, he will give what he swore. If the sale is not valid in its entirety, or he says: it has been consumed, the seller shall pay the clear evidence, and the oath is upon him. The buyer"
21252,"(21252) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: Two men are disagreeing about a sale. There is no agreement between them. He said: The sale will be returned if they are not settled, even if they do not have the agreement between them."
21253,"(21253) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he was asked about bees when riding, and he said: Not. With something"
21254,"(21254) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad hated to make a mirror thing permissible without making it suffice. With it"
21255,"(21255) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his followers, that Abu Al-Khalil recommended that the His wife, Nahal, used to treat her out of embarrassment."
21256,"(21256) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whatever man marries a woman on a friendly basis or a promise, then he is hers if it was before the marriage contract, or if it was love. Her family are lovers after the marriage contract, so it is theirs, and the most worthy of what a man has been honored with is his daughter and sister. (Abu Dawud 213; Ahmed 122)"
21257,"(21257) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Muammar, That he used to judge it, and that Ayas used to judge it."
21258,"(21258) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, that Shurayh and Ibn Udhaynah were not It permits the jilwa."
21259,"(21259) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I asked his leaders about Atiyya al-Jalwawi, he said: This is what he heard. It is not permissible."
21260,"(21260) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man whose wife appears to him, and they say: We will not see you until you have removed anything from her. He said: It is obligatory for him. It is taken. With it"
21261,"(21261) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Uqba bin Amr Abu Masoud came to Then, when he guided you, he said: What is this? They said: The one for whom you interceded. He said: Take her out. Do I seek the reward of my intercession in this world?"
21262,"(21262) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I asked Abdullah about illicit things, and he said: A man asks for a need and it is fulfilled for him, so he brings a gift to him and he accepts it."
21263,"(21263) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Kulayb bin Wa’il, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A large tax collector came to me and said: Accept me from the worker. I do not accept it if I give you something on his behalf, unless the worker believes in him and is troubled by his needs. So I only tarried. For a little while, he brought me my newspaper and said: May God reward you, and he made me ride on his mount and gave me money, and clothed me, so he said: Have you seen that if you had not accepted it, he would have given it to you? I said: No. He said: It is not suitable for you."
21264,"(21264) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Two of the black ones of the Kufa came. Abdullah bin Jaafar sought his help in something against Ali. He said: So he spoke to Ali, and he fulfilled his need. He said: So he sent Al-Dhaqan for forty thousand and something along with it. I don’t know what it is? When it was placed in the hands of Abdullah bin Jaafar, he said: What is this? It was said to him: The Commander of the Faithful sent her with her to whom you spoke about your need. He said: Return her to him, for we O people, we do not sell what is good."
21265,"(21265) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: I witnessed it, and a man came to him and said: I wrote a subscription against this man, and two men with him: Which of them I wish, I have taken my rights, so the man said My friend was in the market and said: Take whichever you want."
21266,"(21266) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: I underwritten for two men in a sale, that He greeted you over your dead and your master over your destitute. He said: It is permissible, and Amr bin Dinar and Suleiman bin Musa said it."
21267,"(21267) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he was asked about a group of people on whom a deed would be written: Which of them will take all of his rights? He said: He is subject to his condition. Whoever of them wishes can take all of his rights, and Abraham liked to take from all of them. A person among them has his share, and he is more just."
21268,"(21268) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who has the right over a people. He says: Whichever of them I wish, I have taken all my rights. He said: This is his status. The sponsor"
21269,"(21269) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahm, who said: I wrote down a statement of truth upon a number: Whichever of them I wish I took my rights, so I presented them to Shurayh, and he said: Take whichever you wish."
21270,"(21270) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say about the servant who was authorized to Commerce: If he was in debt and his master freed him, he said: The servant will strive for them in his debt, he will not increase it. Emancipation is only righteous."
21271,"(21271) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who gives permission to his servant, and he is redeemed, then his master frees him. He said: His master guarantees the value, and Sufyan said: He follows up on his debts with what remains of the debt."
21272,"(21272) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who goes bankrupt and his master frees him. His emancipation is permissible, and the master guarantees his price."
21273,"(21273) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If his master frees him, then the debtor On her master"
21274,"(21274) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He strives for the fines, he did not Freeing him only increases goodness."
21275,"(21275) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a slave is condemned without the permission of his master, then If he is freed, he will be sold for that debt."
21276,"(21276) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: Concerning a slave who buys and sells without his master’s permission. He said: There is nothing owed to his master. He is under the responsibility of the slave. If he is freed, then he is responsible for it."
21277,"(21277) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: Hammad was asked about a slave who was bought without permission. His master freed him, and he does not owe anything, and their property is on the slave’s slaves when he is freed."
21278,"(21278) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Omar, who said: If it is a garment, he returns half the tenth, and if it is He returned the tithe early."
21279,"(21279) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh: In the same way."
21280,"(21280) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Ali, who said: He will not return it. But it will be broken and the defective value will be refunded."
21281,"(21281) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: If a man buys a slave girl, then an ill woman appears with her. It was with the seller. He said: It was obligatory for him, and the seller did not return anything to him."
21282,"(21282) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz that he agreed to it and did not He responds to something."
21283,"(21283) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning a man who buys a slave girl and she has an illness, and he has sex with her before he sees that. He said: I would love to It is removed from him as much as that, and it is permissible for him."
21284,"(21284) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He did not set a time limit for it. Something that destroys what he sees of its appearance."
21285,"(21285) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If she is a virgin, return the tenth. If it was a garment, he returned half the tenth."
21286,"(21286) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: He returns ten times with it. dinars"
21287,"(21287) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, conveying this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A present person cannot be sold to a past person. (Bukhari 2140, Muslim 18)"
21288,"(21288) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. Leave the people and God will provide for them, some of them from others. (Muslim 1158, Tirmidhi 1223)"
21289,"(21289) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Muslim Al-Khayyat told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the sale of a city to a land. (Bukhari 2159. Ahmad 2/42)"
21290,"(21290) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurra, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in buying from the Bedouins. To the Bedouin, he said: Then it was said to him: So he would buy from him for the immigrant? He said: No."
21291,"(21291) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Khayyat, he heard Abu Hurairah say: He forbade the sale of Hadhir to Bad. Ibn Umar was heard saying: A present person should not sell to a stranger."
21292,"(21292) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A present person should not sell to a past person. (Ahmed 420)"
21293,"(21293) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is nothing wrong with him today, but The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to harm people other than the people of the desert when he came to Medina. Ata’ said: No. It is good today."
21294,"(21294) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas, who said: A present person should not be sold to a past person."
21295,"(21295) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The immigrants used to hate selling Hader Labad, and Al-Sha’abi said: And I will not do it."
21296,"(21296) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar said: Show them the way. And tell them the price."
21297,"(21297) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Daghfal, who said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz was read to us: A present person will not sell. Felt"
21298,"(21298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, who said: I said to Ata’: Some Bedouins are approaching us. So should I buy for them? He said: No problem."
21299,"(21299) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fuyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was astonishing for them that they were hit One of the Bedouins is cheap"
21300,"(21300) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: We were forbidden to Hader Labad is sold, even if he is his brother to his father and mother. (Bukhari 2161, Muslim 21)"
21301,"(21301) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard him say: The price of a dog is forbidden."
21302,"(21302) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Masoud, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the dowry of a transgressor and the price of a dog."
21303,"(21303) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace regarding the dowry of a prostitute, the honey of a stallion, the earnings of a cupper, and the price of a dog. (Ahmad 2/500, Daraqutni 72)"
21304,"(21304) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I see Abu Sufyan, he mentioned it on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, for the price of the dog. (Tirmidhi 1279 and Abu Dawud 3773)"
21305,"(21305) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu al-Muhazam, on the authority of Abu Huraira: They disliked the price of a dog, except a hunting dog. (Tirmidhi 1281, An-Nasa’i 6264)"
21306,"(21306) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the dowry of a prostitute, the earnings of a cupper, and the price of a dog.
(Bukhari 2086 and Abu Dawud 3477)"
21307,"(21307) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Qais bin Habtar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who narrated it, He said: The price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of wine are forbidden. (Abu Dawud 3476. Ahmad 1/235)"
21308,"(21308) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The most vile gain is that of the piper, and the price of The dog"
21309,"(21309) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Farwa, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla says: I don’t care about the price of a dog I ate, or the price of a pig."
21310,"(21310) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Al-Hakam and Hammad paying the price of a dog."
21311,"(21311) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abd. Allah bin Qariz, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Zayd, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The cuppers’ earnings It is evil, the wealth of a transgressor is evil, and the price of a dog is evil."
21312,"(21312) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the price of a hunting dog."
21313,"(21313) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no problem with the price of a saluki dog."
21314,"(21314) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you kill a dog He is not a slave, so pay a fine to his family for his price."
21315,"(21315) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, he said: The people were They pay forty dirhams for the dog."
21316,"(21316) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Ismail bin Justas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: In For a hunting dog is forty dirhams, for a livestock dog is a sheep’s sheep, for a plowing dog is a handful of food, and for a dog A house is a piece of dirt. It is the right of the one who acquired it to give it to it, and the owner of the dog has a right to accept it."
21317,"(21317) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the price of a hunting dog."
21318,"(21318) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Talq ibn Muawiyah, who said: I had a man who owed me three hundred dirhams, so I disputed with him. Shurayh, and the man said: They promised me that they would do good to me. Shurayh said: Indeed, God has commanded you to return the trusts to Hello, he said: He ordered her imprisonment, and I did not ask him to imprison him until he made an agreement with me on one hundred and fifty dirhams."
21319,"(21319) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, that he was imprisoned in Religion"
21320,"(21320) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Sariyya Ash-Sha’bi, also called Umm Ja’far, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said : If I am not held back by the debt, then I have fulfilled my rights."
21321,"(21321) Zayd bin Hubab and Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ghalib al-Qattan, on the authority of Abu al-Muhazim: That a man He came to Abu Hurairah about a debtor of his and said: Lock him up. He said: Abu Hurairah said: Do you know how much money he had and he took it? With it? He said: No. He said: Do you know of a large property that he owns? He said: No, he said: What do you want? He said: Lock him up. He said: No, but I will let him search for you, for himself, and for his family."
21322,"(21322) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa and Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he ruled like this. The saying of Abu Hurairah."
21323,"(21323) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hasan bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir: that Ali was imprisoned in debt."
21324,"(21324) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, who said: I witnessed a prisoner who severely imprisoned Rustum in Religion
 Waki’ said: We have never encountered any of our judges, Ibn Abi Layla and others, except that he was locked up in debt."
21325,"(21325) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ali said: There is no imprisonment from the obligations of God. Except for weapons or livestock. (Bayhaqi 163)"
21326,"(21326) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah said: There is no imprisonment except in a ra’a’, or Weapon"
21327,"(21327) Waki’ and Ibn Abi Za’idah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Muhammad came and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace in the sale of confinement."
21328,"(21328) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to imprison the horse. And weapons in the way of God."
21329,"(21329) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father: Al-Zubayr made a waqf for him on the return side of His daughters"
21330,"(21330) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: That Ali and Umar gave land to them as endowments for a period of time."
21331,"(21331) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, who said: Uthman said: The four In Mecca, our children will live there, and those they love will live there."
21332,"(21332) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Imprisonment in the same place as emancipation, is for God in the abode. And real estate."
21333,"(21333) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar invaded the land of Khaybar, so he came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: I have acquired land in Khaybar. I have never acquired more wealth than I have. So what do you command me to do? He said: If you wish, you can keep the originals and give them in charity. He said: So Omar gave them in charity, saying that the originals would not be sold, nor given away, nor He is inherited.
(Bukhari 2737, Muslim 1255)"
21334,"(21334) Abu Khaled and Hafs told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Talhah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I have made my wall for God, and if I could hide it I would not reveal it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make it Among the poor of your family. (Bukhari 1461, Abu Dawud 1686)"
21335,"(21335) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Did you not see that Hijr al-Madari informed me, that Concerning the truth of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, its people eat from it with what is reasonable and not objectionable."
21336,"(21336) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sallam bin Abi Dhayal, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who has land but does not have land. Does he have water to buy water for his land? He said: Yes, there is no problem with that."
21337,"(21337) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, regarding what was read to him about Ata’, he said: I told him: Selling water for Proximity? He said: There is no problem with it. He will draw it from you and carry it. It is not like the surplus of water that flows on the earth."
21338,"(21338) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace regarding the sale of surplus water. (Ibn Majah 2477. Ibn Hibban 4953)"
21339,"(21339) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who Withholding the surplus of water in order to withhold the surplus of water, God will withhold His bounty on the Day of Resurrection. (Abdul Razzaq 14492)"
21340,"(21340) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Umair, he said: A neighbor of mine prevented me from having surplus water, so I asked Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utba? He said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: It is not permissible to sell leftover water."
21341,"(21341) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, he said: It was stolen. The price of water is amazing. Waki` said: This means watering the camel and selling it to the camel."
21342,"(21342) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, He said: It is disliked to sell leftover water."
21343,"(21343) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather: A boy of theirs sold the remainder of their water from their own sheep for twenty thousand, so Abdullah bin Amr: Do not sell it, for it is not permissible to sell it."
21344,"(21344) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, who said: I heard Iyas bin Abdul-Muzani, and he saw People were selling water, and he said: Do not sell water, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding that it should be sold.
(Abu Dawud 3472. Tirmidhi 1271)"
21345,"(21345) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: No. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about withholding excess water in order to prevent pasture. (Bukhari 2353. Muslim 36)"
21346,"(21346) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: There are three whom God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection: a man who withheld the surplus water he had from a wayfarer, and a man who swore an oath. On his goods after the afternoon prayer (meaning: lying) and a man who pledged allegiance to an imam, and if he gives it to him, he will fulfill it, and if he does not give him any of it, then he will not Yep
(Muslim 172. Abu Dawud 3468)"
21347,"(21347) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his mother Amrah, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade preventing the soaking of a well, meaning: surplus water.
(Ahmad 6/1391 Hakim 61)"
21348,"(21348) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: It is not permissible for a blind man to bear witness unless It is something he saw before his sight went away."
21349,"(21349) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qais: that Abu Basir testified with Ali while he was blind, so he turned away. Your testimony"
21350,"(21350) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: The witness of a blind person is permissible."
21351,"(21351) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: He was Shurayh. The blind man's witness is permitted to speak with the just man if he recognizes the voice."
21352,"(21352) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the ruling about the testimony of a blind man? He said: O Lord, something is permissible in it."
21353,"(21353) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he used to permit The witness of the blind man."
21354,"(21354) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih and Israel, on the authority of Isa bin Abi Ezza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that He approved the blind witness."
21355,"(21355) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is permissible for a blind man to bear witness if he is just."
21356,"(21356) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, that his commander testified with Iyas bin Muawiyah, and he was blind. Your testimony"
21357,"(21357) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Abraham about the testimony of a blind man, and he narrated a hadith. We thought he hated him."
21358,"(21358) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Al-Hakam bin Utaiba asked Al-Qasim bin Muhammad about the blind man. Is his testimony permissible and will the people lead? He said: What prevents him from leading the people and bearing witness?"
21359,"(21359) Ali bin Musir and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, that it was not He considers it harmful to buy the hundred in a bid with an offer. He said: Al-Sha’bi said: It should not be bought with an offer, nor by any other means."
21360,"(21360) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he hated it. Hundreds are sold as a gift, except by accident."
21361,"(21361) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Muslim, who said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about buying the extra money for a gift. He said: I do not command it, nor forbid it, nor do I forbid myself and my children, and someone better than me has done that. I said: Who? He said: Commanders of the believers."
21362,"(21362) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Bakr ibn Uthman, who said: I used to buy extra money in Giving in Khurasan for silk and dirhams, so I performed Hajj and asked Salim, and he said: I hate it for dirhams, and there is no problem with gifts. I asked Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi and he said the same, and I asked Ata’ and he said the same, and I asked Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin and they said: We deny it with dirhams, and we see no harm in it with offers."
21363,"(21363) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Dawud, who said: I asked Al-Hasan and Muhammad about the sale of gifts, and they said: : Sell it at an offer."
21364,"(21364) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. On the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Ma`shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: Concerning the mudarib, it is different. They said: They avoid profit and give in charity. With it"
21365,"(21365) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: They give in charity the profit."
21366,"(21366) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: If he disagrees, he is liable, and the profit goes to the owner. Money"
21367,"(21367) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: Profit is based on what they stipulated."
21368,"(21368) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, he said: He is a guarantor, and the profit is between them."
21369,"(21369) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Whoever guarantees money, His profit"
21370,"(21370) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, similar to him, who said: Al-Shu’bi said: They give in charity. Thanks"
21371,"(21371) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Riyah ibn Ubaidah, that a man was sent with him With his goods, when he was on the way, he saw something being sold, so he testified that he was a guarantor of the goods, then he bought it. That is the thing. When the debtor came to the city, he sold the one who had bought it and made a profit. He asked Ibn Umar about that, and he said: The profit goes to the owner of the money."
21372,"(21372) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Ikrimah: Why was he disliked as a cupper? He said: No. He is hated"
21373,"(21373) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: Were it not for the cupper sucking the blood, I would not have seen it. It's unfortunate"
21374,"(21374) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaid Abu Usama, who said: I asked Salim and Al-Qasim about cupping, but they did not see it. And they recited: {Say: I do not find what has been revealed to me forbidden to anyone who tastes it} the verses."
21375,"(21375) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Isa, on the authority of his father, that Uthman ibn Affan said: What I like the beauty of cupping and bathing."
21376,"(21376) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, who said: Al-Harith had a servant who was a cupper."
21377,"(21377) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, that he was asked about the cupping’s earnings. He saw no harm in it."
21378,"(21378) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Haram bin Saad bin Muhaysiah, that his father asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so he forbade him from it, and he did not stop talking to him until he said: Give him fresh water, or Feed your delicate one.
(Abu Dawud 3415. Ahmad 5/436)"
21379,"(21379) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cupped himself. Abu Tayba, so he gave him two Saa’s of food and spoke to his family, so they reduced his burden for him. (Bukhari 6596 and Muslim 62)"
21380,"(21380) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Abu Tayyab measured The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: How much is your tax? He said: Three Saa's. He said: So he took one Saa' of his tax on his behalf and gave him a reward.
(Ahmad 3/353, Abu Ali 1771)"
21381,"(21381) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ata, who said: There was no He sees harm in the cupper's mistreatment of the two camels."
21382,"(21382) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet’s prayers and prayers were cupped. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he rewarded the cuppers, even if it had been forbidden, he would not have given it to him. (Bukhari 2103, Abu Dawud 3416)"
21383,"(21383) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and a boy of his. He said: So I said: O Abu Abbas! What do you do with this tax? He said: I will eat it and I will leave it to you, and he pointed to it with his hand."
21384,"(21384) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Janab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jamil al-Tawwiy, who said: I heard Ali saying: He was cupped. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then said to the cupper when he finished: How much is your tax? He said: Two saa’s. He said: So he took away a saa’ on his behalf, so he commanded me and I gave him a saa’. (Ibn Majah 2163. Ahmad 1/90)"
21385,"(21385) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God was cupped. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rewarded him, and if he had been in need, he would not have given him anything."
21386,"(21386) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali bin Rabah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas. Then a woman came to him and said: I am a woman from the people of Iraq and I have a boy who is a cupper, and the people of Iraq claim that I eat the price of blood. He said: They do not claim anything. You are only eating your slave’s tax, and you are not eating the price of blood."
21387,"(21387) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Farroukh narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ikrimah: The Messenger of God was cupped. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave the cupper his workers a dinar. (Tabarani 7830)"
21388,"(21388) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muammar ibn Sam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: There is no harm in a man using cupping, but not in agreement."
21389,"(21389) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id, who said, I heard Abu Hurairah say: And I was cursed."
21390,"(21390) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were They hate making money as a cupper."
21391,"(21391) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace regarding cupping."
21392,"(21392) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Abdul Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfy: That his father He bought a boy who had a cupper, broke his cuppers, and said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of blood."
21393,"(21393) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that one of his servants from the Ansar had a servant. A cupper, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to put his earnings in fodder for fresh water."
21394,"(21394) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abd. Allah bin Qariz, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Cupping is evil, the dowry of a transgressor is evil, and the price of a dog is evil."
21395,"(21395) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated He won cupping."
21396,"(21396) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: She came A woman went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: I gave my mother in charity to my maidservants, so my mother died and I remained alive. The slave girl, and he said to her: Your reward is due, and she returned to you in terms of inheritance. (Muslim 8050, Abu Dawud 1653)"
21397,"(21397) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, that a man among them gave alms to his mother in charity. So she wrote it down, then his mother died, so Imran bin Husayn asked and said: You inherit from your mother, and if you wish, direct her to her. The face with which you used to face. Hamid said: I saw her being called “Lubbabi.”"
21398,"(21398) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who gives charity, then inherits it. He said: If the Book of God is returned to him, then there is no harm in it. He said: And his leaders said: Ibn Masoud used to say that."
21399,"(21399) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say regarding charity if he inherited it: He said: He makes her look like the face she used to have."
21400,"(21400) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymimi, similar to that."
21401,"(21401) Hisham told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, that he did not see any harm in He ate it."
21402,"(21402) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in eating it."
21403,"(21403) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Eat, for God does not like to feed you unlawful food."
21404,"(21404) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Whatever arrows of the obligatory duties are returned to you, they are yours. halal"
21405,"(21405) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the Awwam, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, that Omar was sincere. He responded to him as he had the right to direct her as she was."
21406,"(21406) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he returns it to him by right, then there is no problem."
21407,"(21407) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who gives charity, then inherits it. He said: The arrows did not increase anything except lawful."
21408,"(21408) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who gives charity, then it returns to him as an inheritance. He said: He makes it from someone else’s share."
21409,"(21409) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mazari’, who said: I asked Al-Shu’abi about it, and he said: If he takes it, there is no problem, but if he spends it, I prefer"
21410,"(21410) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will make it like it."
21411,"(21411) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said, Omar said: Al-Sa’ibi and Al-Siddiqah For their day.
(Abdul Razzaq 14229)"
21412,"Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad told us Ibn Abi Shaybah said:
 (21412) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Concerning a man who lends dirhams to another man and then takes food for their value: he hated him."
21413,"(21413) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, Hammad and Ikrimah, they said: They were not They see harm in that."
21414,"(21414) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If the basis of truth is religion, do not take from it. Except for what you sold him for. If it is a loan, it does not harm you if you take something other than what you lent him."
21415,"(21415) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no problem if a man owes another man dirhams and he gives him So he sued him and said: Take for your rights some barley, or wheat, or dates, or something other than gold. He said: If it is gold. A loan, for he can take it as he pleases."
21416,"(21416) Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, who said: I sold carrots for a dirham until the harvest, and when it came I asked for wheat, barley, and salt, so I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: It is not appropriate. Do not take anything except dirhams."
21417,"(21417) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If a man has a right over another debt, so there is no harm in him buying a cheap slave from him."
21418,"(21418) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Hafs Abi Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Abiyya, that Ali said: There is no problem in giving money in debt and taking it in exchange for two Africans."
21419,"(21419) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Hafs Abi Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Abiyya, on the authority of Ali, similarly."
21420,"(21420) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr that they did not see any harm. That the money is taken in the land of Hijaz and given in the land of Iraq, and that it is taken in the land of Iraq and given in the land of Hijaz."
21421,"(21421) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not see any harm in it."
21422,"(21422) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Miskin and outside, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, that He used to take money in Hijaz and give it to him in Iraq, or in Iraq and give it to him in Hijaz."
21423,"(21423) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad used to take dirhams in Hijaz and give them to him. In Iraq"
21424,"(21424) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not see any harm in paying dirhams. With insight, and they took it with Kufa."
21425,"(21425) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in saftajiya."
21426,"(21426) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Yazid bin Jadbiyah, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq, on the authority of Zainab Al-Thaqafiyya, the wife of Abdullah, said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a judz of fifty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of dates. Barley, and Asim bin Adiy said to her: If you wish, you can fulfill her here in Medina and take her to Khaybar, and she said: Until The Commander of the Faithful asked Omar, and I asked him, and he said: How is the guarantee? (Abdul Razzaq 14643)"
21427,"(21427) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that Ibn al-Zubayr used to give money to merchants here. And he takes from them another land, so it was mentioned, or I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: There is no problem as long as he does not stipulate it."
21428,"(21428) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a sword, and it was Maymun ibn Abi Shabib hated it."
21429,"(21429) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of a dinar. He said: I asked Al-Hasan: I give the money-changer a dirham in Basra. And he took the money, he took something like my money with the money, and he said: He is doing that for the sake of thieves, there is no good in a fixed loan. Beneficial"
21430,"(21430) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: It is permissible for boys to bear witness against one another. Some"
21431,"(21431) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih: He used to allow boys to bear witness, some of them to sell others."
21432,"(21432) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he used to say: It is permissible to say Boys, and their first statement will be taken into account."
21433,"(21433) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Ibn Abbas in Shahadat al-Subyan: God Almighty said: {Among the martyrs you are pleased with} but they are not among those whom He is pleased with. Ibn al-Zubayr said: They are better off if they are asked about what they saw. That they bear witness, and Ibn Abi Mulki said: I did not see that the decrees were taken except according to the words of Ibn al-Zubayr."
21434,"(21434) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not permissible for children to bear witness over adults, but it is permissible Children bear witness to one another when they are separated."
21435,"(21435) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to allow young boys to testify in their age. And the clarifier, and they refuse anything other than that."
21436,"(21436) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Maryam, who said: I heard an alcoholic person saying: When a boy reaches the age of five Ten days passed your testimony."
21437,"(21437) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Dawud ibn al-Husayn, who said: A boy testified before a judge from The judge of the people of Medina, called Salama bin Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzoumi, so he sent for Salim and al-Qasim and asked them about Your testimony, they said: If it grows, then your testimony is valid."
21438,"(21438) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said regarding the testimonies of the two boys: It is written their testimony and they will be steadfast."
21439,"(21439) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: They will be proven."
21440,"(21440) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not permissible for a child to witness."
21441,"(21441) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is not permissible for even minors to bear witness. They grow up."
21442,"(21442) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sahl, on the authority of Amir, who said: He did not allow the testimony of a young boy."
21443,"(21443) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Hamdani, he said: I witnessed With Shurayh, and I am a boy, and he said: With his finger on part of my body: until you reach puberty."
21444,"(21444) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Two young boys from the neighborhood who had not yet reached puberty testified with Ibn Abi Laila, and he said: Write: So-and-so and so-and-so testified while they were children and had not yet reached puberty. When they reach puberty, if they confirm their testimony, it is permissible, but if they return, it is not permissible. With something"
21445,"(21445) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that it was He confirms the testimony of the boys and sends to them and asks them about it."
21446,"(21446) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shurayh, that he permitted two young men’s witnesses in A mother, and he decided on it for four thousand."
21447,"(21447) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, that he used to permit The two boys testified against each other."
21448,"(21448) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Ubaid bin Al-Abras, that Ali guaranteed a carpenter."
21449,"(21449) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Abi Sa’id, who said: I heard Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj narrating Omar Ibn Al-Khattab was among the craftsmen who assisted the people in their works as long as they were destroyed in their hands."
21450,"(21450) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, that he was a guarantor of the butcher’s and jeweler’s, He said: People are not fit for anything other than that."
21451,"(21451) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Shuraih, that he used to guarantee Al-Qassar, and he said: Give him his clothes, or they bought him."
21452,"(21452) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq and Shurayh, he said: They used to guarantee The fuller bought it on the day he took it."
21453,"(21453) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq and Sharih, that they both said about a palace that was broken. A garment: He guarantees its value and takes his garment to him."
21454,"(21454) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he said regarding the short-changer if he spoils it, he said: He is a guarantor, he said: He was not safe from drowning, burning, or an arrogant enemy."
21455,"(21455) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: A neighbor of mine who is a shortsman called Thabit ordered me to ask him: Ibrahim: On the authority of a man who gave his servant a garment and it lost it, so I asked him and he said: Did he not know that it was his servant? I said: Yes, he said: He is a guarantor."
21456,"(21456) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Abraham about a weaver who walked around spinning with a torch of fire. Then sparks fell and burned the yarn. He said: “Damn.”"
21457,"(21457) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyā told us, on the authority of the ruling, he said: The dyer, the butcher, and everyone is liable. Joint worker."
21458,"(21458) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir and Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: The full man is not liable except for what she has committed. That's it"
21459,"(21459) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, that A mother came to some people and deceived them, and claimed that she was free. Then a man married her, and she bore children by him, and they found her to be a mother. So Omar decided to pay the value of her children in every deceitful matter."
21460,"(21460) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, that a mother came to have sex and claimed that she was free. So a man married her, and then her master prevailed over her, so Uthman decided that she and her children should be her master’s, and he made her husband Whatever He took of His possessions, and made among them the Sunnah, or religion: in every head, it has two heads."
21461,"(21461) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I asked him about a female slave who stayed from one land to another. Another land. She went to a people and claimed that she was free. A man desired her and married her, and she bore children. Then they learned that she was His mother, then her master came and took her. He said: The master will take his female slave, and the father will ransom his children with the greatest reward."
21462,"(21462) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Shayba bin Nisah, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, He said: There is deceit in the child of every arrogant person."
21463,"(21463) Muhammad Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar, on the authority of Abbad bin Saeed, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz, He said: Whoever sells a slave, or a man under interdiction, I will give him his money."
21464,"(21464) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the people of its market come to it, inform them that it is a stone. It is not permissible for anyone to mix with him."
21465,"(21465) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man quarantines his slave in the presence of the people of his market, it is not permissible. Aliyah"
21466,"(21466) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he did not see anything in the stone."
21467,"(21467) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Bakkar Al-Anazi, that a man placed a stone on his servant. It was brought to Ali and he said: Did you send him a dirham with which he could buy meat? He said: Yes, he said: So he made him his authorized representative."
21468,"(21468) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A free man shall not be placed under interdiction."
21469,"(21469) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I saw Sharih and a man came to him, and his nephew was with him. He took hold of him, and the man said: My nephew eats a lot of sugar, and he likes to drink. Shurayh said: Hold on to him. His wealth, and he spent on it honourably. He said: His nephew had grown out of his beard."
21470,"(21470) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah, who said: Najdi was written to Ibn Abbas. He asked him about the great sheikh whose intellect had gone away, or whose intellect had been denied, so he wrote to him: When he had gone His intellect, or he denies his intellect, he will be interdicted."
21471,"(21471) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, something similar to that."
21472,"(21472) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to refute those who The utter fool."
21473,"(21473) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zayd Abi al-Mu’alla, a mawla of Banu Tamim, who said: I saw Iyas bin Mu'awiyah and he disputed with him about his maid, and the man said: I bought a maid from this and found her to be a fool! He said: I don’t know how he would be rejected from foolishness. He said: He is as foolish as madness. He said: So he said to her in Persian: Do you remember? What night were you born? She said: Yes, he said: So he said to her: Which of your legs is longer? He said: So she said with one of her legs: This. He said: So he turned her back."
21474,"(21474) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir in Al-Hawj, he said: It is not rejected from it unless it is A known thing. It means: well-known foolishness."
21475,"(21475) A partner told us, on the authority of a sheikh of saffron, on the authority of Masruq, that he used to return from baldness."
21476,"(21476) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him narrating that a man bought from A young man, and when he left with it, he found a knock on it. He disputed with his friend to Sharih, he said: So he said: I bought from this. The boy has a baldness, so look at his baldness, for the baldness does not occur. He said: Then Shurayh said: I do not agree to be a judge or a witness. Show him someone else, then bring them to me and let them bear witness to you. Otherwise, he will swear to God: He did not sell you this lot."
21477,"(21477) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that Ibn Umar and Zayd ibn Thabit were not They see harm in buying one’s livelihood when the coins come out, and that is: zakat, and they say: Do not sell it until you receive it."
21478,"(21478) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: I was informed that Hakim bin Hazzam was He buys a livelihood certificate, but Omar forbade it from selling until he receives it."
21479,"(21479) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, in a similar manner."
21480,"(21480) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: Amer was asked about selling one’s livelihood and he said: There is no problem. With it, but do not sell it until he takes possession of it."
21481,"(21481) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to hate selling one’s livelihood when the deeds were issued."
21482,"(21482) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan: He used to hate it and say: He does not come to the same person, and he says: They are measuring the grapes, and he says: Buy a named measure to Fixed term"
21483,"(21483) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salam bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim: He hated selling one’s livelihood until he received the instrument."
21484,"(21484) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he hated selling one’s livelihood until he took possession of it."
21485,"(21485) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a slave among three people, one of them wrote to him and said: What was taken from him will be taken from him and divided among his partners. And the servant is among them, it is not permissible to write it down. He said: Ataa used to say: He is subject to the effect of his emancipation, as is the case with the one who freed him."
21486,"(21486) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about offices. He was among three people, some of whom boycotted him, and some of them adhered to his writing and did not boycott him, and the one who wrote it died and left behind some money. A lot, who did you leave it to? He said: Then Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Those who adhered to the remainder of their scripture will be repaid, and then what remains will be among them."
21487,"(21487) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a servant who was between two men. So one of them wrote down his share, but Hammad disliked it, and the judge did not see any harm in it."
21488,"(21488) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir: Concerning a man who wrote down his share of a slave, he said If his companions knew about it before he performed it, it would be rejected, and if he did it, it would not be rejected."
21489,"(21489) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amir, about a slave among three, and two of them freed him. Then the slave died and he had money. He said: The one who emancipated the one who did not emancipate will be fined a third of its price, then his inheritance will be divided among him. Three shares, each man one share."
21490,"(21490) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a servant between two men. He said: It was disliked for one of them to write about him except with the permission of his partner. If he did, he would share it. He who did not write down everything was taken from him, so if he who wrote it completes what he wrote down, he will be freed and strive to do it. Half of its value is not written down, and loyalty is between them."
21491,"(21491) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi and Ibrahim, who said: If a man dies and owes a debt... Yes, his religion is permissible."
21492,"(21492) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; Concerning a man who dies and owes a debt for a period of time, Ibn Sirin said: If the heirs make a bond to the owner of the right, then they have the term of their owner. Al-Hasan said: If he dies, his religion is permissible."
21493,"(21493) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: If a man dies or becomes bankrupt, then what he owed is permissible."
21494,"(21494) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man dies or becomes bankrupt, then what is permissible is permissible. Aliyah"
21495,"(21495) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Aban bin Abdul Aziz, Ibn Shihab, and Abi Bakr bin Muhammad and Saad bin Ibrahim used to pay off his debt for a period of time."
21496,"(21496) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If he is trusted The heirs are for his term."
21497,"(21497) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no condition for a dead person."
21498,"(21498) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that he used to hate selling ghee and selling oil, and he would raise For such and such circumstances, and he says: No, except by morning or weight."
21499,"(21499) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he hated qatar. Ibn Aoun said: Qatar A man sells to another and gives some weight to the circumstances."
21500,"(21500) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayal, who said: I asked Ibn Sirin about the one who sells He sells the goods by the weight of the whole package and the packages are with it."
21501,"(21501) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, and Abi Hashim, who said: About a man buying ghee or honey on the condition that he pay for such and such conditions, so they claimed that it was disliked."
21502,"(21502) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked Abraham about a Bedouin who brings grammar from ghee, and he sells it and gives it to the bean-eater, and he says: There is no harm in it."
21503,"(21503) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’a, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit Indeed, he considered freedom from every defect permissible."
21504,"(21504) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salem, that Ibn Umar sold a servant of his for eight hundred A dirham, he said: Then the buyer found a defect in it, so he disputed it with Othman, so Othman asked him, and he said: I sold it for sale, and he said: Do you swear to God: I have sold it, and do you know of any defect in it? He said: I sold it for the sake of exchange. He said: Swear to God: I sold it and what defect is there in it, do you know it? He refused to take the oath, so Othman turned him back to him and sold him after that for one thousand and five hundred dollars."
21505,"(21505) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever defect he named, he was cured of it."
21506,"(21506) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If he names Bara’, he said:"
21507,"(21507) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Concerning a man who sells an animal and says: I am free from such-and-such, I am free from such-and-such, I am free from barefoot. He said: No, and he said: I am free from such-and-such. He said: No, and he said: It is not free. Except for something that He names and shows."
21508,"(21508) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Dinar, who said: I said to Al-Hasan: I will sell the goods and heal myself of sores, wounds, and secretions. And the inner and the outer, so he said: You are not exonerated until you say: In this eye is such-and-such, and this is so-and-so, otherwise it will be returned to you."
21509,"(21509) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is not cleansed of a defect until he names it and removes it. May his hand be upon him."
21510,"(21510) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Azraq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If he is named, he is innocent, even if he does not lay his hand on the defect."
21511,"(21511) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: He will not be healed until he gives birth. May his hand be upon him."
21512,"(21512) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he said: I sell you meat for By God, I will sell to you as long as the land is scarce. He said: When he calls the name, he will be innocent."
21513,"(21513) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Abu Sa`id, they said: : Whoever hires a worker, let him know his reward. (Abdul Razzaq 15023)"
21514,"(21514) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sahl al-Siraj, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: Uthman said: Whoever hires a worker So let his reward be made clear to him."
21515,"(21515) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked that The worker is employed until his wage is made clear to him."
21516,"(21516) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, that he disliked for a worker to use something he did not know. It is nothing, unless it is something known."
21517,"(21517) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The hired worker is not hired. Except with known differences."
21518,"(21518) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who buys a slave girl and the seller says: I will not give her to you until she menstruates. So she was placed in the hands of a servant and she died. He said: It is from the seller’s money."
21519,"(21519) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, that he was asked about a man who bought a slave girl and claimed that she She was pregnant, but the one who had sold her denied it, so they placed the slave girl in the hands of a just man until her pregnancy was discovered, so she died, and he said: If If it is clear that it is charged, then it is from the seller’s money, and if it is not clear that it is charged, then it is from the buyer’s money."
21520,"(21520) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and the ruling regarding a man who sold a slave girl to another man and obtained a defect. So they placed her in the hands of a judge, and she died. They said: This is from the seller’s money."
21521,"(21521) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I witnessed the angels of Abbas bin Tammam bin Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, and with us Ikrimah, so they brought almonds and sugar to scatter it. He said: Ikrimah: Bring it to us on plates, so let us take some of it. Our need"
21522,"(21522) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in using the fangs at weddings and banquets."
21523,"(21523) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to like to bring it on plates. They will get what they need from him."
21524,"(21524) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he saw no harm in it."
21525,"(21525) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: The boys take him."
21526,"(21526) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid, who said: He was called Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila went to a wedding, and they brought sugar to scatter, so he said: Divide it among them."
21527,"(21527) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd Al-Ansari, who said: She witnessed An estate was brought, and sugar was brought to disperse it, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla said: They summoned him and divided him among them."
21528,"(21528) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd. Al-Khattamiyi, in scattering the walnut, said: If you spread it, we will get some of it, and if you spread it, we will not get some of it."
21529,"(21529) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: I encountered righteous men who were hated. He ate what we scattered."
21530,"(21530) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated the risk of marriage. And sugar. He said: And Amer said: There is no problem, he only disliked it as long as his companion did not like it."
21531,"(21531) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Masoud al-Ansari, that When children were scattered about, he would prevent his own children and buy them for them."
21532,"(21532) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Khaled bin Saad, that Abu Masoud The one who forbids drunkenness against boys."
21533,"(21533) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’bi told us, about the ruling, he said: I was between Ibrahim and Shu’bi, and they were asked about The one who prohibited drunkenness at a wedding, Ibrahim hated it, and the people did not see any harm in it."
21534,"(21534) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He did not see anything wrong with it, and Abraham hated it."
21535,"(21535) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, that he disliked spreading drunkenness."
21536,"(21536) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’: He hated the spread of drunkenness."
21537,"(21537) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dhani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abi Al-Sahba’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud: He was asked about it? He said: Singing, and there is no god but Him."
21538,"(21538) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Singing and buying The singer"
21539,"(21539) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is singing, and singing is part of it, and listening To Him"
21540,"(21540) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: And Singing"
21541,"(21541) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, who said: I heard Ikrimah say: It is singing."
21542,"(21542) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is singing."
21543,"(21543) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, who said: It is singing."
21544,"(21544) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is singing. And the like"
21545,"(21545) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Mujahid and Ibrahim, he said Ibrahim: Singing causes hypocrisy to grow in the heart. He said: And Mujahid said: {And among the people is he who buys the meaning of hadith}. Singing"
21546,"(21546) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Al-Miswar bin Zayd narrated to us, that a woman had intercourse. As a boy, she spent on him until he grew up, then she asked for her maintenance, so he wrote about that to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he wrote: She is asked to swear that she did not spend on it seeking the reward of Allah, so if she swears, she will ask for help."
21547,"(21547) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who spends on a foundling, he said: He has nothing to do with it."
21548,"(21548) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: The outcast is free, even if he asks for it. He paid us his usury, and if he was solvent, he would return it to him, and if he was not solvent, then what he spent on him would be charity."
21549,"(21549) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said, Khalid bin Abi al-Salt informed me, he said: Omar told me Ibn Abd al-Aziz: Omar Ibn al-Khattab ruled regarding the child of adultery that he should retaliate against his companion for what he served him, and for whatever remains he should be satisfied with it. And I decided: He should be repaid for what he served him, and what remains I paid him on his behalf from the treasury."
21550,"(21550) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: A man led a camel astray and found it with a man who had spent it. Ali, he fed him and made him fattest, so they disputed with Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who was at that time the governor of Medina, and he decided. To the owner of the camel for his camel, and he ordered him to pay maintenance. Al-Sha’bi said: I did not like that, so he said: The man takes his camel, and we do not spend on it."
21551,"(21551) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Murra narrating Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I saw Ali building a shelter for the strays, and he was feeding them fodder that did not make them fat or make them weak. The house of money, and it was overlooked by its necks, so whoever establishes a clear proof of something will take it, otherwise he will leave it as it is. He sold it, and he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: If I were in charge of the affairs of the Muslims, I would do like this."
21552,"(21552) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one I love most with their purchases is selling the number."
21553,"(21553) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Tawus, that he hated selling the number, and he said: I hate it. To adorn my goods with lies."
21554,"(21554) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to say: A man picks up his belongings. He wants, then he says: I only numbered it to bargain with you for it, then he sells it at a tender price: ten for nine."
21555,"(21555) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: I asked Useful and spring, so I said: We buy the fine linen, then we add more to it than its price, then we price it on it, then we sell it. It is profitable, and we do not explain the increase. He said: No, these are deceptions and lies."
21556,"(21556) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in making a tattoo. The clothes, then he says, “I sell this to you for a profit.”"
21557,"(21557) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, on the authority of Al-Hikam, that he said that, and he said: It is only Similar to bargaining"
21558,"(21558) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man claimed a mule in the hand of a man, and he set The clear that it is his, and he established the clear that he produced it, so he decided with a share of that. He is in His hand."
21559,"(21559) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: A dispute was made to Abdullah bin Utbah regarding the governorship. And I am with him, so each one of them established the proof that it is his. He said: I saw Abdullah bin Utba moving them. In his hand and says: This is for the one who is born, this is for what is in his hand."
21560,"(21560) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: A mule was found in Al-Nahrain, so he stayed The clear difference is that it is theirs, so Abdullah bin Utbah ruled on it: for the one who paid back their hands."
21561,"(21561) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the two proofs are equal It is for what is in their hands."
21562,"(21562) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If two witnesses testify, that this animal belongs to so-and-so. And it was produced with him, and two witnesses testified that it belonged to so-and-so, and it was produced with him, so it is for the one in his hand."
21563,"(21563) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who has a garment in his hand, so the man evaluates what is clear that it is his garment, and he evaluates what is in his hand. The clear evidence is that it is his garment, so he said: it is for the one in his hand, and he said about the animal: this clear proof is that it is His animal, and the one who is in his hand evaluates the clear fact that it is his animal. He said: It is for the one in his hand."
21564,"(21564) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, that two men claimed a camel, and each of them stayed One of them is clear that he is his, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that he is between them. (Abu Dawud 339; Abd al-Razzaq 15202)"
21565,"(21565) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abi Al-Darda', that two men disputed with him over an animal, and each one of them established clear evidence that it was his, and he decided on it. He came between them and said: The more of you is not in need of the chain of the Children of Israel. (Abdul Razzaq 15204)"
21566,"(21566) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of Abu Musa, that two men quarreled on a horse, so each of them stood up. One of them was clear that it was hers, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided it between them.
(Abu Dawud 3608, Hakim 94)"
21567,"(21567) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of his servant, on the authority of Saeed."
21568,"(21568) Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abi He saw that two men disputed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a mount, but he did not have anything to explain to them, so he ordered them to do so. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked them to turn to the right. (Abu Dawud 3661, Ahmed 489)"
21569,"(21569) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about the gift of a man who had money from a man, so when It was loosened. He said: He caught it as a speculator. He said: It is not right until he takes it from him, then gives it to him if he wants."
21570,"(21570) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A deposit is like a loan. You do not pay its Mudarib until You are arrested"
21571,"(21571) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, about a man who had money for a man and said to him: Buy it for him. He said: There is no problem, but if the one for whom he bought it perishes, then I explain to him that it was for him that he bought it, otherwise he will not believe that it is for him. He bought it for himself, and if it was speculative, then he should not buy anything with it until he takes possession of it or gives it to her. His guardian"
21572,"(21572) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is forbidden if a man owes a debt. He submits to him about something until he takes it."
21573,"(21573) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who owed another man a debt and he surrendered him to him. He said: No, not until he arrests him."
21574,"(21574) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Mudaribs are disbursed. In debt, and the debt is not spent in Mudaraba."
21575,"(21575) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Kulayb bin Wa’il, who said: I heard Ibn Umar being asked about a man who had There was a man who was in debt, and he wanted to give him something to eat, but he thought about it and said, “No, not until he takes it.”"
21576,"(21576) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Uthman that he made a ruling regarding the garment. A man bought it and there is a defect in it that means he should return it if he had worn it."
21577,"(21577) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who bought a garment and then saw something defective in it, he said: He will deduct from its price whatever he removes that defect."
21578,"(21578) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: He used to say; Concerning a man who buys a garment and sees defects in it. He said: He used to say: If it changes from its condition, I would love to He will reward him and reduce the amount of shame from him."
21579,"(21579) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh: Two men disputed over him. One of them bought a narrator from the other, cut it up, then found a flaw with it and said: What you told about it is worse than what was. With it"
21580,"(21580) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the arbiter, about a man who bought a garment, cut it up, and found fault with it. He said: : He returns it. I asked Hammad and he said: He will return it, and he will return the cutting tools. Shu`ba said: And Al-Haytham told me, on the authority of Hammad, that he said: The burden of the poor will be removed from him."
21581,"(21581) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Jabala ibn Suhaim, who said: I saw Ibn Umar buying a shirt and wearing it. Then yellowish matter struck him from his beard, so he wanted to return it, but he did not return it because of the yellowness."
21582,"(21582) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Uthman, he said: Whoever bought a garment He found a flaw in it, so he made the choice."
21583,"(21583) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdul said: The Most Gracious: growth with security, meaning profit."
21584,"(21584) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih; Concerning a man who returns a slave with a ransom, he said: He returns it, and he has the burden."
21585,"(21585) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, that a man bought a slave and took advantage of him, then a man came So he summoned him, and he disputed with him to Iyas bin Muawiyah, and he claimed justice for him, and he ruled for him for the slave and for his female mule, and he ruled for the man against his companion. The one who bought it from him for the likeness of a slave and for the likeness of his female slaves. He said: So I mentioned that to Muhammad bin Sirin, and he said: He understands."
21586,"(21586) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who bought a slave and discovered a defect and took advantage of it. He said: The cost is for the buyer."
21587,"(21587) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The price is guaranteed."
21588,"(21588) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli: Concerning a man who bought a house and took advantage of it, then a man came. So he deserved it, he said: I will not make it any burden, meaning the one who deserves it.
 And similar to this, it is about someone who rescues whoever is in his power."
21589,"(21589) Waki’ and Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Mukhlid ibn Khuffaf, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that the tax is subject to guarantee. (Abu Dawud 3502. Tirmidhi 1285)"
21590,"(21590) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said to him: The price is due to the guarantee."
21591,"(21591) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Layya, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib: Concerning a man who sold a house to his son, The father was exhausted, so the son came to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so he annulled his sale and decided to take possession of the house for him, and he said: What are your crops? He said: I made it hard by guaranteeing it."
21592,"(21592) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of a man called Hajjaj, on the authority of Shurayh: In A man took advantage of a slave and took advantage of him. He said: He returns the ransom."
21593,"(21593) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Yasar, That Zayd bin Thabit and Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam did not see any harm in a man buying what was on the tops of palm trees if he acquired it, then He sells it on the tops of palm trees before it is harvested."
21594,"(21594) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that He hated it"
21595,"(21595) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad, that he said: If a man buys dates on the tops of palm trees, He will not sell it until he receives it."
21596,"(21596) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikramah, that if he bought the fruit on the tops of palm trees, he was reluctant to sell it until Yasramha"
21597,"(21597) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who buys dates on the tops of palm trees, he said: There is no harm in selling them before To crush him. He said: And Muhammad did not see a difficult time in him, so when they attacked him during that time, he said: Leave what makes you suspicious for what does not cause you doubt. He makes you suspicious."
21598,"(21598) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn al-Furat al-Ansari, who said: I sold a garment to a people and took a mortgage from them. He begged us for a term, and when the term came, I bought a palm tree from them for what I owed it, and took it and dried it on the tops of the palm trees, and it fell. Some of it was ripe, so I took it, then the people who had sold it came to me, and they wanted the fruit to come to me, so I sold it to them for a term. Most of the people were interested in that, so I asked Salim and told him the story, and he said: Was it your intention to sell it to one of them? I said: No, by God, and it did not occur to my heart. He said: There is no problem. He said: I asked Al-Qasim and he said: Did you intend to sell it to them? I said: No, by God, and it did not occur to my heart. He said: No problem."
21599,"(21599) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Harun ibn Musa al-Nahwi, who said: Al-Zubayr ibn Khairit informed me, on the authority of Ikrimah Concerning a man who buys the fruit of a palm tree, he said: He will not sell it until he has harvested it."
21600,"(21600) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade About the second.
(Muslim 1175. Ahmad 313)"
21601,"(21601) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: I said to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: I sell dates. I am satisfied or excluded? He said: Do not exclude anything except known trees, and do not disavow charity. He said: I mentioned it to Muhammad bin Sirin and it was as if he liked it."
21602,"(21602) Ismail bin Aliyah and Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Had it not been that Ibn Umar He hated the second person and was well accepted by us. We did not see any harm in that. Ibn Aliyah added, on the authority of Ibn Aoun: We spoke that Ibn Umar used to say: I will not sell this palm tree, nor will I sell This palm tree"
21603,"(21603) Abbad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that he hated to buy something. Of palm trees by measure."
21604,"(21604) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: I said to Abraham: I will sell the sheep to the man and he will exclude some of it. He said: No, but say: I will sell you half of it."
21605,"(21605) Abd al-Samad bin Abi al-Jaroud told us, he said: I asked Jabir bin Zayd about a man who makes a sale and excludes it. Some of them said: This is not suitable."
21606,"(21606) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who sells his land for dates and excludes the trees. He said: It was a wonder for him to grow palm trees."
21607,"(21607) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa about a man. A man sold goods and said: I am a partner in them. He said: He thought about this sale."
21608,"(21608) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Amr bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim, that he hated to be excluded. By measure, or baskets, or kilograms."
21609,"(21609) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: He sold the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace and deliver a camel and set a condition for its back to Medina. (Bukhari 443. Abu Dawud 3499)"
21610,"(21610) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of His father sold his fruit for four thousand and excluded eight hundred dirhams from it."
21611,"(21611) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’, on the authority of Salim: He did not see any harm in selling it. Its fruit, and a known measure is excluded from it."
21612,"(21612) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Bashir, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: We bought a second from Ibn Umar and he excluded Some of it"
21613,"(21613) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He did not see any harm in selling it. A man, his fruit, and he excludes a third, a quarter, or a half."
21614,"(21614) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Rijal, on the authority of his mother Umrah: She used to sell the fruit of her land and exclude it from it."
21615,"(21615) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather: He sold his fruit for four thousand dirhams, or for three, and he excluded seven hundred from it."
21616,"(21616) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in selling it. The commodity excludes half of it."
21617,"(21617) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Rabi’ al-Ra’i, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: He sold Its fruit, and it is excluded from it."
21618,"(21618) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: There was something wrong with Abraham’s wife. So he ordered me to give it to her for the value of dirhams, dinars."
21619,"(21619) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar He has the paper, so he gives its value in dinars, if it is based on a price, and he has dinars, so he gives The paper is worth its value."
21620,"(21620) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Al-Bayhi, on the authority of Yasar bin Numayr, on the authority of Omar: He did not He sees no harm in extracting gold from paper, and paper from gold."
21621,"(21621) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Nafi’, who said: I asked Sa’id bin Jubayr about a man who took a piece of paper. Or a piece of gold as a loan. He said: There is no problem with it."
21622,"(21622) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: He did not see any harm in it."
21623,"(21623) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri and his followers, that they said: There is no harm in that."
21624,"(21624) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in extracting gold from paper and paper from gold. At market value."
21625,"(21625) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him."
21626,"(21626) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: There is no harm in him."
21627,"(21627) Ibn Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, that he did not think it was wrong for a man to have A man owes dinars, so he takes dirhams from him and exchanges them, and he sees no harm in adding to the price or subtracting from it. If it was by mutual consent."
21628,"(21628) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: He used to hate it. Gold is made of paper, and paper is made of gold."
21629,"(21629) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he hated to be given Gold is made of paper, and paper is made of gold."
21630,"(21630) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Ubaidah ibn Abdullah ibn Masoud: Do not take gold from paper, it will be yours over a man, and do not take paper from gold."
21631,"(21631) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked you about a man who lends money. A man takes dirhams and takes dinars from him."
21632,"(21632) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah: He hated it."
21633,"(21633) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: Concerning a man who had money from another man. So he took from it, then he wanted to take its value of dinars, so he thought of it."
21634,"(21634) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: Ata’, the servant of Omar bin Abd, informed me Al-Aziz, he said: I bought a camel from the slave of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab for four dinars, and he came to seek his rights from me. So I said: I have dirhams, but I do not have dinars. He said: Until I asked Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab for advice. So he asked him and he said: Take it from him. A certain amount of dinars, but if he refuses, then let him. God’s promise is to him."
21635,"(21635) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I have been informed that Ibn Masoud He hated it"
21636,"(21636) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah, similar to him."
21637,"(21637) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, who said: I asked Musa bin Talha and he told me that Othman Khabbab gave land, Abdullah gave land, Sa`d gave land, and Sahib gave land, and each of my neighbors I saw gave him his land. A third and a quarter: Abdullah and Saad."
21638,"(21638) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him his land. By Khaybar means half."
21639,"(21639) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, who said: There were Saad and Ibn Masoud. They farm a third and a quarter"
21640,"(21640) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Muadh came to us while we were giving our land for a third and a quarter, but he did not frown. That is upon us."
21641,"(21641) Ibn Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Muadh, something similar."
21642,"(21642) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: He worked with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The people of Khaybar took control of the half, then Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman and Ali, then they took them back and to this day they are given a third And a quarter"
21643,"(21643) Abu Usama and Waki` told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Uthman, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I asked him about the farms. For a third and a quarter, and he said: If you look at the family of Abu Bakr, the family of Omar, and the family of Ali, you will find them doing that."
21644,"(21644) Ibn Abi Zaydah and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Kulayb bin Wa’il, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A man who owns land. And water, and had no seeds or cows, so he gave me his land in half, so I planted it with my seeds and cows, then I divided it among the half. He said: Good."
21645,"(21645) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Husayra, on the authority of Sakhr bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Amr bin Sulay’, On the authority of Ali: He did not see any harm in farming on half the farms."
21646,"(21646) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Anas, who said: My land and my camel. Either way"
21647,"(21647) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who heard Salim say: He defeated Rafi’ bin Khadij over himself, by God. We will make you feel like a camel."
21648,"(21648) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha al-Qannad, who said: I heard a peacock saying: There is no harm in farmers receiving half and a third. And a quarter"
21649,"(21649) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad: He used to farm for the people of Al-Sawad. His father's life"
21650,"(21650) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Amir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, who said: I used to farm for one-third. And a quarter, and I will carry it to Alqamah, and the lions. If they saw any harm in it, they would have refrained from it."
21651,"(21651) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed: that Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to order that the land be given for a third And a quarter"
21652,"(21652) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’: that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote to Adi to farm By a third and a quarter."
21653,"(21653) Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Qasim, and Ibn Sirin: They did not see any harm in A man gives his land to another on the condition that he gives him a third, or a quarter, or a tenth, and he does not have to pay any expenses. Something"
21654,"(21654) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: My father did not see anything wrong with renting land."
21655,"(21655) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid, who said: I asked Salim about it and he said: There is no problem with it."
21656,"(21656) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, On the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, he said, Zayd bin Thabit said: May God forgive Rafi’ bin Khadij, I, by God, know best the hadith from him. Two men came to him who had fought, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is your business, so do not invade the farms. Rafi’ heard his saying: Do not invade the farms. (Abu Dawud 3383, Ahmed 182)"
21657,"(21657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: There are no people in Medina. The house of Hijra except that they will give their land for a third and a quarter."
21658,"(21658) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He used to pay his land By a third"
21659,"(21659) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zaid, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: My land and my camel are the same."
21660,"(21660) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace The governor of the people of Khaybar greeted the governor. (Muslim 1186. Abu Dawud 2999)"
21661,"(21661) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, he said: It was for Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Abi Layla acquired land in Al-Fawwarah, and he used to pay a third and a quarter for it, and they would send me their apportionments."
21662,"(21662) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: He forbade us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a matter that was beneficial to us, forbade us, if one of us had land, from giving it to some of us. Its tax is a third, or a half. He said: And whoever has land, let him cultivate it, or let him give it to his brother. (Tirmidhi 1384)"
21663,"(21663) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I asked Ibn Maqil about farms? He said: Thabit bin Al-Dahhak told me: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade it. (Muslim 1188 Ahmed 33)"
21664,"(21644) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he heard Omar narrating, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade Intelligence
(Muslim 1177. An-Nasa’i 4651)"
21665,"(21665) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Amr heard Abdullah bin Omar say: We used to tell people, but we did not see any harm in that. Rafi’ ibn Khadij even claimed that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade it, so we abandoned it for its sake.
(Muslim 1179. Abu Dawud 3382)"
21666,"(21646) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, who said: It was forbidden. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of intelligence. I said: What is intelligence? He said: To take the land for half, or a third, or a quarter. (Ahmed 187 Abd bin Humaid 253)c"
21667,"(21667) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas was in the Sacred Mosque, when a man came to him and said: We are taking the land from the people, so I will occupy it with my seeds and my cows. So he took He fulfilled my rights and I gave him his rights, so he said to him: Take your capital, and do not add anything to it. So he returned it to him three times, each He says this to him."
21668,"(21668) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Ikrimah: He forced farmers to pay a third and a quarter."
21669,"(21669) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim: He forced farmers to pay a third and a quarter."
21670,"(21670) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked giving him the land for a third or a quarter."
21671,"(21671) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that he disliked renting land."
21672,"(21672) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Do not bury the land or its seed, or he said: How much?"
21673,"(21673) Waki’ told us, he said: Omar bin Dhar told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Rafi’ bin Khadij, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Rafi’ came to us from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us about a matter. He was kind to us, and he obeyed God and obeyed His Messenger. He was kind to us. He forbade us from cultivating any of the land except land he owned. Her neck, or a gift given to her by a man. (Ahmad 465. Abu Dawud 3390)"
21674,"(21674) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Nusayr ibn Adham, who said: I heard al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim saying: No part of the land is fit except Two properties: land given to you by a man who owns its property, or land that was leased for a specified fee for a specified period."
21675,"(21675) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The most representative of the doors The farmer is to rent the white land for a known fee."
21676,"(21676) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no suitable for cultivation except land. She owns her own property, or a land granted to her by a man."
21677,"(21677) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Rifa’i bin Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: The Messenger forbade God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding farms and renting: except when a man buys land, or lends it, and then says: He lent land to my father. From a man who planted it and built a structure in it, then he went out to it and saw the structure and said: Who built this? They said: So-and-so whom you lent, and he said: Should I compensate for what you gave him? They said: Yes. He said: I will not leave until you destroy him."
21678,"(21678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no harm in renting land for food."
21679,"(21679) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a man to rent white land. With wheat"
21680,"(21680) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, who said: I asked Sa’id bin Jubayr about leasing the land in dirhams. And food, and he saw no harm in it."
21681,"(21681) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in taking food. Named"
21682,"(21682) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ya’la? Hakim, on the authority of Sulaiman Ibn Yassar, on the authority of Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. Or let his brother cultivate it, and he should not force it for a third, or a quarter, or with the specified food. (Muslim 113. An-Nasa’i 4623)"
21683,"(21683) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: There was an animal in the hands of the people of Azd. Then a group of people claimed it, and they established the proof that they had led them astray in the time of Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz, so those who established it It is in your clear evidence that we sought counsel, so that matter was submitted to their judge, Abd al-Rahman ibn Adhinah, and he made These people will go in the morning with a clear statement, and the others will leave with more than them. So he wrote about that to Shurayh, and he wrote to him: I am not Of idle talk and multiplying over anything, and those who have established clear evidence that they seek refuge while it is in their hands is more deserving. And those are more worthy of resemblance."
21684,"(21684) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, about two men calling on an animal not in hand. One of them, so two witnesses appointed one of them, and the other had four, so he said: There are two halves between them, because the two They oblige the truth."
21685,"(21685) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He is among them according to the quotas of witnesses."
21686,"(21686) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf: That Hisham bin Hubaira used to judge most of the two groups. Witnesses"
21687,"(21687) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim Ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ka’b, who said: I sold a mule to a man, so he stayed for a while. As God willed, he came to me and I recognized the mule with him. So he came to Shurayh and she set off on the animal, and seven witnesses appeared. His animal was not sold, nor was it given to him, and the other brought six witnesses that his animal was not sold, nor was it given to him. Then Sharih said: I bear witness that one of the two parties is a liar, so he divided it among them into thirteen shares, which he gave to each one of them. According to the testimony of your witnesses."
21688,"(21688) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Hanash ibn al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Ali, who said: He disputed There were two men among his mule, so he appointed five witnesses as witnesses that it had been produced with him, and this man appointed two witnesses. Because it was produced with him, so Ali made it among them for weeks."
21689,"(21689) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the slave authorized to do business becomes bankrupt. So his debt is on his neck, so if his master wants to sell it to him, he will sell it to him, and divide its price among the creditors, but not on him. More than its price."
21690,"(21690) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If they want to sell it, they will sell it, and if they want Seek help"
21691,"(21691) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he used to say: If they want, they can sell it, and if they want They sought help from him, he said: And Shurayh used to say that."
21692,"(21692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: It should not be sold until the debt is paid. With your neck"
21693,"(21693) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah was given A servant who was in debt rode on him and said: His money is due to his religion, his money is due to his religion."
21694,"(21694) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: His debt is for its price."
21695,"(21695) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A slave cannot be sold on credit, even if he owes a hundred thousand."
21696,"(21696) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Hassan bin Amr told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The servant strives to The debt is not sold."
21697,"(21697) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih; Concerning a man who gives permission to his servant to borrow money. He said: He wanted to be sold to the debtors."
21698,"(21698) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman: He used to say about the man He buys goods and finds something defective in some of them. He says: Take it all, or return it all."
21699,"(21699) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Amer: Concerning a man who buys goods. Then he finds a defect in some of it. He says: Take it all away, or return it all."
21700,"(21700) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, who said: If a man buys two boys or two goods He found a defect in one of them and wanted to return it. He returned it for its value, and the one without a defect was rewarded."
21701,"(21701) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who buys slaves and finds a flaw in some of them. He said: It will be returned for its value, and the goods are the same, and Muhammad said it."
21702,"(21702) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Shurayh: Concerning a man who buys goods in bulk. Then he finds fault with some of it. He says: Take it all away, or return it all."
21703,"(21703) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amer, and Ibn Sirin, who said: If a man buys and sells a piece of property and sees in it A defect, they said: He returns it all."
21704,"(21704) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who bought goods and found some of them defective. He said: : He returns it and is obligated to pay the remaining value."
21705,"(21705) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Yasar: That a man bought alleys of ghee from another man and exchanged His companion, the bottle was closed, and he wanted to pay him some dirhams, so Ibn Omar said: Take all of your sale, or return it all."
21706,"(21706) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Mudarib spent all the money, and Ibn Sirin said: Not like that."
21707,"(21707) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The mudarib spends and hoards. In a reasonable manner, if he wins, it is from his profit, and if he puts in, it is from the capital. He said: I asked Ibn Sirin, he said: I do not like to spend without asking permission from the owner of the money."
21708,"(21708) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If the speculator wishes, he can hire the worker and feed the slave if he is one of the Mudaraba, and he does not eat with them."
21709,"(21709) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The Mudarib does not stipulate food, nor anything that he will benefit from except If there is a benefit in it for the Mudaraba, then if there is no benefit in it for the Mudaraba, then it is money. Himself"
21710,"(21710) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Lahia, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salem: He asked them about a lender who eats, drinks, wears clothing, and rides in a reasonable manner. He said: If it is for the sake of speculation, then no. Unfortunately"
21711,"(21711) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The intercessor has more right to the intercession of his neighbor, and he will wait for her, even if he is absent, if their paths are the same.
(Abu Dawud 3512. Tirmidhi 1369)"
21712,"(21712) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: He ruled that pre-emption was granted to the partner after ten days. For years her companion was absent."
21713,"(21713) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to see Al-Shafi’i for the young and the absent."
21714,"(21714) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Shurayh: In the house you buy it and for it. A pre-emptor is absent, or a minor. He said: The absent is more deserving of pre-emption until he returns, and the minor until he grows up."
21715,"(21715) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no intercession for someone who is absent. Al-Harith used to see that."
21716,"(21716) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam, who said: There is an intercessor for the absent person."
21717,"(21717) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: For the absent person, an intercessor is written. If he takes it and sends the price, otherwise there is no intercession for him."
21718,"(21718) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, he said: Their statement came to the point that Taking over is a sale."
21719,"(21719) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: Taking charge is a sale."
21720,"(21720) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Taking possession is a sale, and do not take possession of it until it is received."
21721,"(21721) Hafs and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Al-Hikam, who said: Taking charge is a sale."
21722,"(21722) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he did not see By assuming power."
21723,"(21723) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Taking charge is a sale."
21724,"(21724) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Taking charge is a sale."
21725,"(21725) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Taking charge is a sale."
21726,"(21726) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hazn ibn Bishr, on the authority of Raja` ibn al-Harith: That a man made a mistake in A servant who had returned, so he took him to return him, so he kept away from him, so he disputed with him to Sharih, so he took him to him, so he reported that to Ali, and he said: He has wronged. Judgment, he swears to God: it will remain from him, and there is no guarantee on it."
21727,"(21727) Ali bin Musir, Abdou and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who took A slave was left to be returned, so he left him and said: There is nothing wrong with him."
21728,"(21728) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is nothing upon him."
21729,"(21729) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, that a man took a freed slave and kept him. From him, he said: The slave’s master came and presented him to Shurayh, and Shurayh said: He has left you before him, so there is nothing against him."
21730,"(21730) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Ibn Abi Malikay said to me: If it goes away from him, then it is not There is something wrong with him"
21731,"(21731) Muhammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of his leaders, Abu Hashim, and Mansour. They said: If he flees from the He took it and there is no guarantee on it."
21732,"(21732) Yahya bin Abi Zayd and Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Ghani, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Food was presented to Uthman according to the promise of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Take us to Uthman and we will help him. He sold his food, and Othman stood beside him and said: In this gharar, such-and-such, and sell it for such-and-such. Likewise, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whatever you name, then eat.” (Abdullah bin Hamid 52, Ahmed 75)"
21733,"(21733) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: If the measure and weight are named, do not sell them. Even its weight."
21734,"(21734) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, and Al-Hasan, that they said: When he named the measure and the weight Let him eat it."
21735,"(21735) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you submit in peace and name a trustee, do not take haphazardly"
21736,"(21736) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, who said: If you buy food in its size, eat it. That means if you buy it by measure."
21737,"(21737) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He hated to give him any of the food. Until he arrests him."
21738,"(21738) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers: He saw no harm in taking over food before he He pauses and says: He is well-known."
21739,"(21739) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: He hated it."
21740,"(21740) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Wahb the blind, on the authority of Ata’: He did not see any harm in He is his guardian before he takes him."
21741,"(21741) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed, who said: Whoever buys something by a measure, Or its weight, so he will not sell it until he takes possession of it, and he sees no harm in putting it in charge or sharing it with anything other than One measure, no weight."
21742,"(21742) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he narrated it, He said: There is no harm in following Allah and polytheism before it is fulfilled. (Abdul Razzaq 14257. Abu Dawud 198)"
21743,"(21743) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Hizam bin Hakim, who said: He said to me: Hakim: I bought food from the food of charity and profited from it before I took it, so I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I asked him? He said: Do not sell it until you receive it. (An-Nasa’i 6195 and Tayalisi 1318)"
21744,"(21744) Ali bin Musir and Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, both on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you buys food, he should not sell it until it is a measure of it. Ibn Abu Zayed: And he will be rewarded. (Muslim 1161, Bukhari 2124)"
21745,"(21745) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I asked him about salaf in oil. And ghee, wheat, and barley? He said: There is no harm in it, but do not sell it until you receive it."
21746,"(21746) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I was informed that Hakim ibn Hazzam used to buy He issued a deed of livelihood, but Ibn Umar forbade it to be sold until he takes possession of it."
21747,"(21747) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, similar to the hadith of Ayyub."
21748,"(21748) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If you buy a sale forever, then You follow him until you capture him."
21749,"(21749) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: If you buy Do not sell food until you have received it, and he does not see any harm in polytheism, or you have given him the price."
21750,"(21750) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata: A man who buys something, then He sells it before he takes possession of it. He said: No, until he takes possession of it."
21751,"(21751) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ibrahim being asked about a man who sells goods. Before he arrested him? He said: This was only in terms of measure and weight."
21752,"(21752) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The food that was forbidden is not It is sold until it is seized, and I consider everything like food."
21753,"(21753) Muhammad bin Maysar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Kharijiyah Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Thabit : He used to forbid those who buy a neighbor’s newspapers until they have finished with them."
21754,"(21754) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever buys food should not sell it until he eats it. I said to Ibn Abbas: Why? He said: Don't you see that they are buying gold and food that is postponed? (Bukhari 2132. Muslim 29)"
21755,"(21755) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Othman told us, he said: Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj told me, On the authority of Sulayman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever buys food should not He sells it until he buys it. (Muslim 1162. Ahmad 337)"
21756,"(21756) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Ali { And give them of the wealth of God which He has given you. He said: A quarter from the beginning of its stars. (Ibn Jarir 129)"
21757,"(21757) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He disliked that A man leaves his office until he is at the last star, for fear of being unable to do so."
21758,"(21758) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Ibn Sirin used to like to write in letters when writing. The Book, and I make you lower than the last of your stars."
21759,"(21759) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The offices are given to him by a quarter of all his correspondences, which she expedites. From your owner"
21760,"(21760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Shabib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: that Omar wrote a servant to him. He was called Abu Umayyah, so he surprised him with his star when he came and said: O Abu Umayyah, seek help from him in your correspondence, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you leave him until he is at the last star, he said: I fear that I will not reach that time, then he recited: {And give them of the wealth of God which He has given you}"
21761,"(21761) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to marvel at them. To leave to write to him a group of his letters."
21762,"(21762) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: In the words of God Almighty: {And give them of the wealth of God which He came to you. He said: Of what God has provided for you from His correspondence."
21763,"(21763) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: You give him whatever you like with which you are not satisfied. A temporary thing."
21764,"(21764) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Mujahid, they said: It will be removed from him."
21765,"(21765) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {And give them of the wealth of Allah which He has given you} He said: from what is in it. Your hands"
21766,"(21766) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman: He wrote to a boy and gave him a quarter, and he said: This is the saying of Ali: {And give them of the wealth of God which He has given you}"
21767,"(21767) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Adi bin Al-Fadil, who said: I went to Omar bin Abdul-Aziz and dug a well for him. He said: Her harem is fifty cubits long, and he has no right to a Muslim, nor is he harmed by it, and the wayfarer is the first to drink."
21768,"(21768) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: I asked Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, About giving? He said: As for the people of the pre-Islamic era, it was fifty cubits on its side, and there was a hundred between the two wells, so when it was Islam saw that something other than that was sufficient, so each well was made twenty-five cubits, and its two sides were fifty cubits."
21769,"(21769) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, who said: The harem of the well is forty cubits in its entirety, not No one may enter upon him either his perfume or his water."
21770,"(21770) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, who said: The harem of al-Badi’ was twenty-five cubits. The harem of the ordinary is fifty cubits, and the harem of the plantation.
 Al-Zuhri said: And it has informed me that the harem of the spring will be a hundred cubits long."
21771,"(21771) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. On the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The length of the well is forty cubits."
21772,"(21772) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The harem of the Well of the Beginning is twenty-five cubits, and the harem of the ordinary well. Fifty cubits, Sa`id said, and the harem of Bir al-Dhahab is three hundred cubits. (Abu Dawud 402. Hakim 97)"
21773,"(21773) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Aws al-Absi, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya al-Absi, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is no fever except in three cases: the third of the heart. It means the harem of the well and the people’s ring. (Bayhaqi 151)"
21774,"There is a person whose son is a manager, a boy who has offices with us, and he left and came to his office instead of writing his father's letter, so he is left, so this is a ruling."
21775,"(21775) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays ibn al-Ahnaf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: Concerning the man He sells his servants to his master, saying: Whatever his master takes is his, and whatever remains is nothing to him."
21776,"(21776) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais ibn al-Ahnaf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, with a similar example. Hadith of Abbad, except that he said: There is nothing for you if your companion dies."
21777,"(21777) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Dawud bin Harith told me, he said: I witnessed a scribe who ruled on that."
21778,"(21778) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Abu Awan, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: What is left will be taken from him."
21779,"(21779) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ayyub and Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The manager is not sold except by himself."
21780,"(21780) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He was reluctant to sell it, but he did not see it. It is unfortunate that he should write it."
21781,"(21781) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The services of the manager are not sold except to the one who Himself"
21782,"(21782) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’: That Ibn Umar was in his care as an orphan, so he married her off. And he gave her money to her husband, Mudaraba."
21783,"(21783) Ibn Abi Zayd and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hamid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Omar bin Al-Khattab had the money of an orphan given to him as a speculator, so he asked for it and was successful, so they divided the credit with him, then they separated."
21784,"(21784) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Omar bin Al-Khattab had an orphan’s property. So he gave him a speculator in the sea."
21785,"(21785) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Ali: He took possession of the property of an orphan and gave it to him. His servant"
21786,"(21786) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the trustee acting with money. The orphan, I said to Abraham: If he turns away, will he be responsible? He said: No."
21787,"(21787) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the successor acting With the orphan's money or his."
21788,"(21788) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He disliked that an orphan’s money be paid in a speculative manner, and he said: Protect it, and do not expose it to land or sea."
21789,"(21789) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said regarding the orphan’s wealth: If you trade If you win it, then it belongs to him, and if it is lost, you are responsible for it, and if you lose it, then it is yours, and it is not your responsibility."
21790,"(21790) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: We were orphans in Aisha’s custody. She used to purify our wealth and sell it."
21791,"(21791) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Fudayl bin Marzuq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: {And do not approach the orphan’s property except with It is better. He said: The orphan seeks his wealth."
21792,"(21792) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, a man from the people of Al-Kufa: That a man said: O Messenger of God, should I kill my orphan? He said: Strike him from what you used to strike your son. He said: What do I eat from his wealth? He said: With kindness, not taking his wealth, nor protecting his wealth with his wealth. (Bayhaqi 285. Tabari 260)"
21793,"(21793) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: What I ate of the orphan’s wealth So it is a debt owed to you. Don’t you see what God Almighty says: {Then when you hand over to them their property, then bear witness against them}"
21794,"(21794) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salama ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubaidah about his saying: {And whoever is rich, let him maintain chastity, and whoever is poor, let him eat reasonably.} He said: It is only a loan. Don’t you see what he said? :{So when you hand over to them their property, then bear witness against them}"
21795,"(21795) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: In his saying: {And whoever is rich Let him maintain chastity, and whoever is poor let him eat reasonably."
21796,"(21796) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the executor needs to, he may put his hand With their hands, and he does not wear a turban."
21797,"(21797) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abdah ibn Abi Lubab, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: In the words of God Almighty: {And whoever is poor, let him eat with reasonableness} He said: from his wealth."
21798,"(21798) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah. And Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, they said: With a loan."
21799,"(21799) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: A woman came to him and asked him, and she said: My children and brothers are descendants of their father and they are orphans in my care, and I had money and I used to spend it on them until He went, and they have money, so what do you see? He said: Place your hand with their hands and eat with kindness."
21800,"(21800) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, and Ikrimah: {And whoever is poor, let him eat with reasonableness}, He said: He puts his hand down."
21801,"(21801) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, in his saying: {And whoever Whoever is rich, let him maintain chastity, and whoever is poor, let him eat reasonably. She said: This was revealed about the one who takes care of the orphan’s wealth. And he corrects him if he needs to eat from it. (Bukhari 45751 Muslim 2315)"
21802,"(21802) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: A woman sent me to him. I ask him about the orphans in whose care she rose over them. Did she eat any of their wealth? He said: Yes, with kindness."
21803,"(21803) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Umm Salama al-Atkiya, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Eat from the orphan’s wealth. And know what you eat."
21804,"(21804) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Aisha said: I do not hate it. That the orphan’s wealth should be naked with me until I mix his food with my food and his drink with my drink."
21805,"(21805) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that he granted permission to the guardian of an orphan to eat instead of doing good deeds."
21806,"(21806) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya al-Azraq, on the authority of al-Sha’bi: Concerning the guardian of the orphan’s wealth: He eats from the messengers and dates at the expense of the wage-earner."
21807,"(21807) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who hired his servant for a year, then he wanted to sell him. He said: He can sell him if he wants."
21808,"(21808) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, regarding a boy who is pushed by a man to another. He teaches him, then takes him out before he fulfills his condition. He said: He returns to his teacher what he spent on him."
21809,"(21809) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of al-Hikam. He said: I asked you about a man who rewarded his servant for a year and he wanted to Does he take it out? He said: He may take it.
 He said: I asked Hammad, and he said: He does not take it except from harm."
21810,"(21810) Shababah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I heard Abu Ad-Duha mention: that Shariha And stolen. They used to say about a man if he rents a slave for a year or a month or the like, and then it appears that it is taken from him: That is for Him."
21811,"(21811) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: A man asked him, and I heard about a man who was entrusted with Did he invest money in it? He said: Ata used to say: Whatever growth is in it is for the owner of the money, and Mujahid said: It is not for the owner of the money or the warehouse. And it is for the needy."
21812,"(21812) Abu Bakr told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Do not move the entrusted animal except with the permission of its Lord. If he does, He is a guarantor, and he has the profit."
21813,"(21813) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abraham, regarding a deposit: There is no guarantee. Unless he shifts it from its place, or changes it from its current state, for if he changes it from its place, So there was a profit in it, so he gave it in charity, but not to either of them."
21814,"(21814) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about the orphan’s wealth? He said: He is guaranteed until He pushes you to Him. He said: Indeed, there was grace in Him. He said: Do whatever you want with His grace. Guaranteed until you pay him to him."
21815,"(21815) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who has money for orphans. So he works with it. He said: He is guaranteed if he does it without their permission, then the profit will be given in charity."
21816,"(21816) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Perhaps a man will surrender to another man. A thousand dirhams or the like, and he says: If you give me wheat then so-and-so, and if you give me barley then so-and-so. He said: Poison of every kind. Some of it is a named piece of paper, so if he gives you what is in it, otherwise take your capital."
21817,"(21817) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam al-Manqari, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr: Concerning a man who greets and says: “It was not.” If you have any wheat, take it like this, and whatever grain you have, take it like this: He hates it."
21818,"(21818) Yahya Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of his father, who said: Amer was asked about peace in wheat and barley. Which of them did he give to him? He said: It is not suitable."
21819,"(21819) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: about a man who submitted to Islam for a known period of time. It is known, and if he does not pay it, then such-and-such for another known thing, he said: It is not suitable."
21820,"(21820) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who pays in advance and says: If it is righteousness, then with this. And if it was barley, then like this: he hated it."
21821,"(21821) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Razin ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab He said: There is no harm in offering peace of clothing for a specified period of time for a specified period."
21822,"(21822) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nashit, who said: I asked Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj about peace in"
21823,"(21823) Ibn Abi Za’idah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, who said: Amer was asked about the ladder in the nightmares? He said: I used to do it."
21824,"(21824) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Amir, who said: If he embraces Islam in a garment, he will recognize its arms and its patch. It's okay"
21825,"(21825) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir and Ata’, who said: There is no harm in peace in wool and clothing."
21826,"(21826) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he was asked about peace in the nightmares? He said: There is no harm in it if it is within a specified period for a specified period."
21827,"(21827) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Masoud did not He sees peace in everything as a means of protection for a specified term, except for animals."
21828,"(21828) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who converted to Islam while being spoiled. Should they be sold before they are fully satisfied? He said: No."
21829,"(21829) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn Al-Harithi, on the authority of Ali, who said: When you follow in the offices Two stars, and he entered the Sunnah and did not return his stars. He was rejected in slavery."
21830,"(21830) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Then, the one who wrote said: You have failed, he replied. Delicately"
21831,"(21831) Waki’ and Ibn Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, on the authority of Ata’: that Ibn Umar He wrote to a servant of his for a thousand dinars, so he paid them back, except for a hundred, and then returned him to the bond."
21832,"(21832) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, who said: If a star enters another star, it becomes clear. His inability"
21833,"(21833) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to refute He is summoned if he is unable and does not seek help from him."
21834,"(21834) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: If his servant wrote for one hundred uqiyas, and he paid for them except ten uqiyahs, then he failed, he returned it. Slavery
(Abu Dawud 3922, Ahmed 206)"
21835,"(21835) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: It will not be rejected until he is unable to do so for years."
21836,"(21836) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If you know the measure of something, do not sell it in bulk."
21837,"(21837) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I said to my father: The man says: I have said such-and-such and such-and-such in this hideout. of us, and I do not know whether it may have been defective, stolen, or something was hidden, or there was a mistake in it. I will not sell it to you for a price, but for I will sell you a lump sum. He said: Ibn Sirin disliked it, but Al-Hasan saw no harm in it."
21838,"(21838) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who spoke unjustly? So he said to him: Whatever wheat is in your house, so and so, and whatever barley is so and so, he said: He thought about it. Abraham"
21839,"(21839) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr: He asked Al-Sha’bi about a group of Bedouins who would come to us with food and we would buy food. A measure of them, then we say: They sold us in lump sum. He said: No, until you abandon the sale."
21840,"(21840) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: He did not see any harm in He sells it in lump sum if he informs him that he knows how much it will cost."
21841,"(21841) Rawad bin Jarrah Abu Issam Al-Asqalani told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said : I asked Al-Hasan, Mujahid, Akramiah, and Ata’ about a man who comes and buys food from his house, and there is a risk in it. Did the food know its worth? Everyone thought about it."
21842,"(21842) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: You have seen us and among us are the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He brings the wasaks and throws them in the prayer area, and the man says: I ate such-and-such, and I do not sell them for measures. I sold it at a risk, but they saw no harm in it."
21843,"(21843) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We used to meet the riders, So we buy food from them at a risk, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from selling it until we move it from its place. Or we move it.
(Bukhari 2166, Muslim 1161)"
21844,"(21844) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, Ash’ath, and Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: In his offices he died, He owes a debt and what remains from his correspondence. He said: He strikes his master with whatever stars he has bequeathed.
Hammad said: They strike with what is permissible what is not permissible."
21845,"(21845) Hafs told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, who said: Shurayh made a mistake, even if he As a judge, Zayd ibn Thabit used to say: He begins with the debt before receiving the letter."
21846,"(21846) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the one who was appointed dies while owing a debt, he strikes his master. With what has fallen from its stars with the debtors, and if there is no star for it, it begins with the debtors and they take their debt, if anything is left over. It belongs to his master until he is summoned, so if anything is left over after being summoned, it belongs to his heirs."
21847,"(21847) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His master strikes with the creditors for whatever he has bequeathed. Your stars"
21848,"(21848) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It begins with religion."
21849,"(21849) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: It begins with religion. (Bayhaqi 333)"
21850,"(21850) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam, that they said: If the debtor is in debt And what remained of his correspondence, he said: He will look at what stars have fallen upon him, and what was for his creditors, and that will be divided. By quotas."
21851,"(21851) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, Sufyan, and Ibn Abi Layla, they used to say: If he dies, it will be upon him. Debt: He pays off what he owes, so the master will multiply the debts with all the debtors."
21852,"(21852) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Shurayh made a mistake, even if He was a judge. Zaid bin Thabit said: He begins with the debt."
21853,"(21853) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father told me: People of understanding quarreled with people of Banu Sulaim went to Marwan, so Marwan ordered Ibn al-Zubayr to judge between them, so the witnesses gathered together. So Abdullah cast lots among them, and he assigned it to the one on whom the lot fell, because the witnesses were unanimous."
21854,"(21854) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If it is straight The two clear proofs belong to what is in their hands."
21855,"(21855) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he said regarding the people if they differ Their martyrdom and they are equal in calibration and number: the oath is upon the one upon whom a supplication is made."
21856,"(21856) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Do not receive, do not celebrate, and do not spend for one another."
21857,"(21857) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Do not Sales made with penny coins."
21858,"(21858) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Daghfal, who said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz was read to us: No. Receive the stirrups."
21859,"(21859) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He forbade receiving a burden, for if a man meets it So he bought it and gave his friend the option when he came to Egypt."
21860,"(21860) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade receiving sales. (Bukhari 2149, Muslim 1156)"
21861,"(21861) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not sell riders. (Bukhari 2150, Muslim 1155)"
21862,"(21862) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Habib, on the authority of Nawfal ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he forbade receiving prayers. (Ibn Majah 2064; Abu Ali 537)"
21863,"(21863) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so that merchandise is delivered from the mouths of the streets. (Tabarani 12, Darqutni 281)"
21864,"(21864) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not upon the one who withdraws, the borrower, or the one who stores it. Guarantee unless violated."
21865,"(21865) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: If the repository and the borrower violate And the one who replaces it is a guarantor."
21866,"(21866) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you forbid your speculator to buy such and such goods Likewise, he bought a guarantee, and Hammad said: They give the profit in charity."
21867,"(21867) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The mudarib is trustworthy, even if he disobeys your command."
21868,"(21868) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: That Omar guaranteed four thousand people who were with him. speculative"
21869,"(21869) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The mudarib is entrusted, even if he violates it."
21870,"(21870) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: I entrusted six Thousands, so they left, and he said: Omar: Did you leave anything with them? I said: No. He said: So he guaranteed me."
21871,"(21871) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muzzam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: If the Lord stipulates The money is on the speculator: It does not descend in the depths of a valley, and it descends, so he is guarantor."
21872,"(21872) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Who divides the profit? There is no guarantee on it."
21873,"(21873) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a mudarib who gave money to someone else, he said: There is no guarantee on him, and he is trustworthy."
21874,"(21874) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Uthman, the son of my brother Shurayh, on the authority of Shurayh, that he said: If he violates In deposits and rent, he is a guarantor."
21875,"(21875) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: In a mudarib, the owner of the money said to him: Do not go beyond a place. Such and such, he said: He is guaranteed if he exceeds it."
21876,"(21876) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, something similar."
21877,"(21877) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Do not stipulate anything from the mudarib, for I fear that he will disobey and harm you and himself."
21878,"(21878) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: He was asked about a man to whom speculative money was given, and he said: No. He left Egypt, so he left and said: There is no guarantee on him."
21879,"(21879) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab: Concerning the mudarib, if they stipulate that: no He exceeds, so he exceeds, so he is guaranteed."
21880,"(21880) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, he said: He is a guarantor."
21881,"(21881) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Ata’. He said: If he forbade He goes out and he goes out, so he is guaranteed."
21882,"(21882) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the repository and the borrower disobey And the one who replaces it is a guarantor."
21883,"(21883) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that Abu Bakr did not guarantee what was deposited."
21884,"(21884) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hilal bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ukaym: A man entrusted a man with trust, and she perished, but his life was not guaranteed."
21885,"(21885) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: There is no guarantee for the person in storage and the borrower except that Orphaned"
21886,"(21886) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith. On the authority of Ash'ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam: They did not see any harm in betting if it was in the hands of a just person and accepted."
21887,"(21887) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said: He is a benefactor."
21888,"(21888) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: It is not a mortgage until he takes possession of it. His companion"
21889,"(21889) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id: He (Farhan Maqdoun) read it, and he said: No. The mortgage is only accepted."
21890,"(21890) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked a man giving him money Mudaraba to give him goods."
21891,"(21891) Ibn Abi Rawad told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father that he hated him."
21892,"(21892) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He was asked about a man who paid speculative money to a man, and stipulated that he Goods? He hated it
 Ibn Sirin did not see anything wrong with it."
21893,"(21893) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin: He did not see any harm in a man pushing To a man, he exchanged money on the condition that he would provide him with goods, or do work for him."
21894,"(21894) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab said regarding Umm al-Wald: Her son set her free, even if he was a miscarriage."
21895,"(21895) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Qarib Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father: He bought From a man who was a slave-girl for four thousand, and she had fallen ill from her master, and that came to Umar, so he brought him and rewarded him with a pearl. He beat him and said: After your flesh was mixed with their flesh and your blood with their blood, you killed them. May God curse the Jews. They were forbidden. They had the fat on them, so they sold it and ate its price."
21896,"(21896) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If the mother becomes pregnant by her master, then she miscarries, he said: If His character was clear, so she was the mother of a child, and there was no way to sell her."
21897,"(21897) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: If he was confused in the fourth creation, then he was created and freed. Mother"
21898,"(21898) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, that they said: If a mother miscarries from her master, then Free"
21899,"(21899) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The mother of the child shall be freed if she has a miscarriage, if it is known. It was a miscarriage."
21900,"(21900) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah: Concerning the mother of the child, if she gives birth to him while he is still chewed, then she has been freed. With it"
21901,"(21901) Jarir told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I asked him, I said: We carry this. Goods for people and we need them on the way. He said: If you come, do you buy what they need for their owners and do not withhold them? I said: Yes, he said: There is no problem, it is better for the owner of the goods."
21902,"(21902) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man to whom dirhams were paid and he bought them with them. He used it for his need, then returned it and bought it for the one he was commanded to do. He said: He is a guarantee until he delivers it to Lord!"
21903,"(21903) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Mahan, who said: Ibn Masoud passed by a man who weighed a single ounce. He said: Give it more weight, and he said: Set the balance straight, and if it is straight, give him as much money as you want."
21904,"(21904) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hudhayl, this is what Abu Al-Ahwas said. He said: I saw Ammar bin Yasser bought a robe and asked for more rope, but he refused to add more, so I saw Ammar dispute with him over it, but I don’t know. Which one of them defeated him?"
21905,"(21905) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Ammar, the same."
21906,"(21906) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Badal Abi al-Wadah al-Shaybani, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali: He passed Aisha had bought meat and she said to him: Give me more, so he said to him: Give me more. This is greater for the blessing of the sale."
21907,"(21907) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in adding more than Selling"
21908,"(21908) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of a man from Nakh`, who said: I saw an Ammar who bought A fight from a man and he disputed with him over a rope, and Ammar said: Give me more, and the other said: No."
21909,"(21909) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of someone who heard Ibn Umar say to him: If you buy meat, do not add more."
21910,"(21910) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Abu Al-Sha’atha’i said: It is not permissible for a woman to give birth until she gives birth. What did they buy?"
21911,"(21911) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: It is not permissible for a woman to give a wife without her permission. Her husband"
21912,"(21912) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If she stays in her house for a year, it is permissible for her to do so. I made it"
21913,"(21913) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If the slave-girl gives birth, or a child like her, it is permissible Oh my God!"
21914,"(21914) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Omar made a promise to me that I would not allow She has a kingdom until she turns one year old in her house, or gives birth to a womb."
21915,"(21915) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: in the same way."
21916,"(21916) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: I read Omar’s letter to Shurayh about that, and that. A female maid of Quraysh said to her, “And she is your kingdom”: Give me your inheritance from your father in charity before You would go to your husband, so she did so, then she asked for her inheritance and he returned it to her."
21917,"(21917) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad, Muhammad said: It is not permissible No woman is free until she turns one year old, or gives birth to a son, and Al-Hasan said: Until she gives birth to a son, or reaches the age of that."
21918,"(21918) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I said to him: What do you think if she is stubborn? He said: No. It is permissible"
21919,"(21919) Ubayd Allah narrated to us on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’ and Mujahid, who said: The orphan has two throats that are not permissible for her. Nothing in her wealth until she gives birth to a child, or spends a year in her husband’s house."
21920,"(21920) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail and Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: Omar said to me: I will not repay your gift. A female slave until she turns one year old in her house, or gives birth to a boy. Ismail said: I said to Al-Shaabi: Do you think that if she is stubborn, it is permissible? He said: Yes."
21921,"(21921) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He saw no harm in the price of a dowry."
21922,"(21922) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Tawus: They hated the price of the feline and sold it and ate it. His flesh and to benefit from his skin."
21923,"(21923) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the price of felines? They said: There is no harm in it."
21924,"(21924) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bought a cat and said: There is no harm in buying it. The price is for the seller."
21925,"(21925) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, who said: I asked Ata’ about him? He said: There is no harm in it."
21926,"(21926) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I think Abu Sufyan mentioned it, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him for the price of a kitten."
21927,"(21927) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir: They both hated the price of a cat."
21928,"(21928) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos ibn Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali sent Muhammad ibn Abi A virgin in Egypt, so he wrote to him asking him about a person who died and left behind wealth and children, so he wrote an order regarding the offices: If He left a legacy in fulfillment of what he wrote to him, and he called his followers, and they were satisfied, and what remained was an inheritance for his children."
21929,"(21929) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I told him: Shurayh used to judge in The one who wrote to him dies and leaves behind money and children. What remains of his correspondence and what remains of his response to him are paid on his behalf to his master. His son? He said: Shurayh was ruling on it according to the ruling of Abdullah."
21930,"(21930) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The surplus of anything belongs to its masters until it is completed. Corresponding to him, and if anything left over after writing to him, it goes to his heirs."
21931,"(21931) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
21932,"(21932) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, that Omar bin Al-Khattab and Zaid bin Thabit said: If the recipient dies and has money, it belongs to his master and his son has nothing."
21933,"(21933) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah: In some offices, he died and left behind money and free children. He said: He will pay what remains from writing to him, and whatever remains goes to his son."
21934,"(21934) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Musisar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: that Abdullah freed him, and he said: As for his property, But it is for you (Abdul Razzaq 15655)"
21935,"(21935) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Anas asked a servant of his about his wealth? So he told him, and he said: You and your money."
21936,"(21936) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulki: A woman from Aisha’s people emancipated a slave, so she asked Aisha and she said: If you emancipate him and do not stipulate his wealth, then his wealth. No"
21937,"(21937) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Umays, on the authority of Imran ibn Umayr, on the authority of his father: that Abdullah freed a servant of his, and he said : As for the money, it is mine, but it is yours."
21938,"(21938) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: That Abu Ayyub called a boy of his and asked him about his money? So he told him and said: You and your money."
21939,"(21939) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If a slave is freed, his property follows him."
21940,"(21940) Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Money is for the slave unless the master makes an exception."
21941,"(21941) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man frees his slave, his wealth follows him."
21942,"(21942) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If A man freed a slave and had wealth, so the slave’s wealth belongs to the slave."
21943,"(21943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If a slave is freed, his wealth follows him."
21944,"(21944) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: Concerning the one who frees a slave and has wealth, he said: I love To make it clear to him, if he wants to keep you, he will keep him, and if he wants to keep him with him, he will make him."
21945,"(21945) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If a man frees his slaves and has wealth, then his wealth To his kings"
21946,"(21946) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If he frees him, the money belongs to the master."
21947,"(21947) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Abi Aoun Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Omar and Ali, who said: If he converts to Islam and has land, we will waive the tax on his behalf and take the tax from him."
21948,"(21948) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy: that Diqan greeted Ali’s covenant and said to him: Ali: If you remain in your land, we will lift the tribute from your head and take it from your land, but if you turn away from it, we will I have more right to it."
21949,"(21949) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn: Two men from the family of Ulysses converted to Islam during the reign of Omar, so they came to Omar. So they informed him of their conversion to Islam, so he wrote for them to Othman bin Hanif to lift the tax from their heads, and to He takes the weather from their land."
21950,"(21950) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab: That Deqan of The people of Nahr al-Malik converted to Islam, so Omar said: Give her her land and she will pay the tax on its behalf."
21951,"(21951) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab: that Deqan She converted to Islam at the expense of the king, so Omar wrote that they should give her a choice."
21952,"(21952) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer: Al-Rufail Diqan al-Nahrain converted to Islam, so it was obligatory for him Omar lived in two thousand years, and he lifted the tribute from his head, and gave him his land to pay the tax on it."
21953,"(21953) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, he said: I asked Ubaid Allah bin Omar about who among the people of black converted to Islam, and he said : Whoever of the people of the Black Lives who is free of charge, he will have his land and property, and whoever of the people of the blacks who is free of charge, he will have his land and property, and whoever of the people of the Black People who is free of charge will submit to Islam, he will only take possession of him. In fact, his land is for the Muslims.
Ubaid Allah said: I read this in the book of Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
21954,"(21954) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man from the people of Sawad converts to Islam, then stays On his land, the kharaj was taken from him, but if he left it, the kharaj was not taken from him."
21955,"(21955) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that someone who was written to had an inability He returned it as a slave and kept what he had taken from it."
21956,"(21956) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: They will have what they took from him."
21957,"(21957) Ibn Abi Za’idah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: He puts it in Like him"
21958,"(21958) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Look how much the people helped him in his correspondence. So He will place him among the slaves, and whatever his earnings and wealth belong to his master."
21959,"(21959) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: He will make it like it."
21960,"(21960) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is for his master.
Sufyan said, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He will put it among the slaves."
21961,"(21961) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Farra, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Abi Tharwan: that Ali urged the people to Ibn al-Nabah, so they gathered for him more than writing to him, so I preferred his preference, so he made her superior to those who wrote to him."
21962,"(21962) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He asked for something for one or two necks, and was given. He gave, and when what he was given was too much in the eyes of Abu Musa, he ordered it and what was given was brought in, then he looked at what he asked about it. So he gave it to him and took the surplus and put it on his neck, or slaves."
21963,"(21963) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Subaih narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Aban, on the authority of Subaih bin Abdullah: Abdullah bin Abbas urged the people to write to him, so they gathered together for him and he fulfilled his call, and there remained a surplus, so Abdullah put it in The clerks"
21964,"(21964) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab: He saw no harm in a man treating the palm trees and treating them with a third and a quarter of what he did not spend of it himself. Something"
21965,"(21965) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to hate it. That is, except for a known reward."
21966,"(21966) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Fudayl, on the authority of Salim, who said: Concerning palm trees, it is given to those who work It is from him."
21967,"(21967) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He disliked everything that was done for a third. And a quarter"
21968,"(21968) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri: He did not see any harm in hiring a hired worker. He works the land for a third and a quarter."
21969,"(21969) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He hated to hire a worker and say: For you. A third or a quarter of what comes out of this land."
21970,"(21970) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Muhammad about a man who pays a third of a garment to a weaver. A dirham, or a quarter, or whatever they agreed upon? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
21971,"(21971) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim: They disliked that he pay The man gave the garment to the weaver for a third. He said: And Ata saw no harm in that."
21972,"(21972) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: There is no problem if he pays one-third to him."
21973,"(21973) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers: He did not see any harm in paying the garment. To the weaver for a third and a quarter."
21974,"(21974) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Marwan bin Muawiyah, who said: I asked Shahr bin Hawshab about the garment he pays. A third or a quarter to the tailor? He said: A condition without a capital."
21975,"(21975) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He disliked giving the garment to the tailor for a third. And a quarter"
21976,"(21976) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, who said: I asked Ayyub and Ya’la bin Hakim about the man who defends Is the garment given to the weaver for a third or a quarter? He saw no harm in it."
21977,"(21977) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: They mentioned the man He is forced to eat the dead, and to take the Muslim man’s wealth. I said: He eats the dead, and Abdullah bin Dinar said: He eats The Muslim man’s wealth was considered permissible for him if he was forced to, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said: You are correct. A dead person is permissible for him if he is forced, but a Muslim’s wealth is not permissible for him."
21978,"(21978) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: If he is forced to do what was forbidden to him, then whatever was forbidden to him, then he It is lawful."
21979,"(21979) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever sells a pregnant woman or frees her and excludes what is in it. Her stomach. He said to him: We praise Him in what His character has made clear, and if He has not made His character clear, then there is no praise for Him."
21980,"(21980) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to permit a double sale, but not He will reward her with emancipation."
21981,"(21981) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: Concerning a man who frees a slave woman and excludes what is in her. Her stomach, he said to him: her tummy."
21982,"(21982) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: They are both Harran."
21983,"(21983) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: He has two companions."
21984,"(21984) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who frees slave women and makes an exception for them. What is in her stomach? They said: He has that."
21985,"(21985) Qurayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Fada’i, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I asked him about a man who was emancipated. The mother and excludes what is in her womb. He said to him: “His”"
21986,"(21986) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who bought a slave and freed him, then he was found with him. Insanity, he said: If the one who pays is before the deal is made, the seller will return to the buyer the surplus between the good and the good, and he will make up what was taken in Like him"
21987,"(21987) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who bought a slave and freed him, then an illness appeared in him, which was With the seller, he said: It was obligatory for him, and the seller would not return anything."
21988,"(21988) Mu’ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He was of the opinion that the defect would be removed from him to the extent of the defect, if it was found. This is an illness after death."
21989,"(21989) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no covenant after death."
21990,"(21990) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli and his companions. On the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The loan is permissible, even if it is for a term, and Abu Bakr takes it with it."
21991,"(21991) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Amir: Concerning a man who marries a mother and she gives birth to him. Then he buys her, they said: He sells her as long as she does not give birth in his possession."
21992,"(21992) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: He will sell it."
21993,"(21993) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: She is the mother of a son."
21994,"(21994) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He will not sell her, for she is in the position of the child’s mother."
21995,"(21995) Mu’ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning a man who gave a man speculative goods, so the value of the goods was a thousand dirhams. Then he sold it for nine hundred. He said: The capital is nine hundred."
21996,"(21996) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said about a man who gave a man speculative property and they settled it. Between them, he said: Capital is what the goods are valued for, and their value is nothing."
21997,"(21997) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Nabatah, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Tawoos: He was He sees nothing wrong with a man exchanging goods for another man and giving them to him in exchange for that value."
21998,"(21998) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazeed, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He hated it. He sold Dawazda, and he said: He sold non-Arabs."
21999,"(21999) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Atiq, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr: He used to hate it. He sold this dādāzdā and this dāzdādah. I said to him: What should I do? He said: Say: I took it for such-and-such, and I will sell it to you for such-and-such."
22000,"(22000) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar Ad-Dahni, on the authority of Ibn Abi Naam, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It is usury."
22001,"(22001) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Maimun, who said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab asked about the sale of Dawazdah? He said: There is no problem with it."
22002,"(22002) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: We used to hate him, then We saw no harm in him."
22003,"(2003) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ibn Sirin, that they said: There is no harm in selling it."
22004,"(22004) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is usury."
22005,"(22005) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ja’d bin Dhakwan, who said: I witnessed a commentator who approved the sale of Dawazdi."
22006,"(2006) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Masruq: He disliked the sale of Dawazdi, he said: He says: I bought it for such-and-such, and I sell it for such-and-such."
22007,"(2007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He hated it, and Ikrimah said: It is forbidden."
22008,"(22008) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is usury."
22009,"(2009) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whatever man she gives birth to is his female slave, then he will be freed from the afterlife.
(Ibn Majah 2515, Darmi 2574)"
22010,"(2010) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, He said: Omar consulted me about selling the mothers of the children, and he and I decided that if she gave birth, she would be freed, so Omar decided for her life and Othman from After him, when I took charge of her after them, I decided to promote her. Al-Sha’bi said: Ibn Sirin told me, he said: I said to Ubaidah: What do you see? He said: The opinion of Omar and Ali in the group is more beloved to me than what Ali said when he realized the difference."
22011,"(22011) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Nafi’ told us: Two men from the people of Iraq asked Ibn Umar about the fathers. They said: We left Ibn al-Zubayr selling the mothers of the children in Mecca. Abdullah said: Abu Hafs Omar, do you know him? He said: Whatever man has a female slave, he will have enjoyment during his lifetime, and he will be free after his death, and either A man had intercourse with his slave girl, then had intercourse with her, so the child is his and the lost one is his."
22012,"(22012) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: A man from the neighborhood died and left behind the mother of a child, and he said Al-Walid bin Uqba sold it, so we came to Abdullah bin Masoud and asked him, and he said: If you will inevitably do it. So make it part of her son’s portion."
22013,"(22013) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, he said: Omar sold Ibn Al-Khattab placed the mothers of our children among us, then he returned them to us, until he returned them to my pregnant women while they were hidden."
22014,"(22014) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The mother of a son came to Ali and he said: Omar has freed you."
22015,"(22015) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, who said: He reported a riot in the army of Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz saw that he had sold the mothers of his children, and a man came to him and reminded him of that, so he saw a more severe age for freeing them. From the man who mentioned that, and Omar thinks that this is the opinion of Omar bin Al-Khattab."
22016,"(22016) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Ibn al-Zubayr sells Mothers of children. Ibn Umar said: But Umar ruled that it should not be sold, given away, or inherited. Its owner should enjoy some of it. His life, so if he dies, he is free."
22017,"(2017) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Amr bin Qais, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah: It was mentioned to him that he sold the mothers of his children, and he said: But Omar, the strong and trustworthy one, freed them."
22018,"(22018) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Uthman made a ruling regarding the child’s mother that she A free woman if she gives birth to her master."
22019,"(2019) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He made the child’s mother a share. Her children"
22020,"(2020) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the mother of a child commits an indecency, he will not be afflicted with it. That being said, she is as she is, and if her master dies, she is freed."
22021,"(2021) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Hasan and Ibrahim did not see the mother of the child being sold. Even if she wants it, and Ibn Sirin was of the opinion that it should be sold."
22022,"(2022) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Sam’a, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, who said: Omar bin Abd wrote Al-Aziz in the child’s mother: She is free, even if she wants."
22023,"(22023) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, he said: The mother of the child does not perform ruqa on her. The event"
22024,"(2024) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The mother of the child shall not be sold, even if It exploded."
22025,"(22025) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: I asked Salim bin Abdullah, or a man asked him, he said: The mother of the child If it becomes ungodly, should I sell it? He said: No, her immorality is against herself, and she is a free woman."
22026,"(22026) Waki’ told us, he said: Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Malik bin Amir. Al-Hamdani, he said: Omar said about the child’s mother: If she is chaste, Muslim, and chaste, she will be freed, and if she is unrighteous, ungrateful, and commits adultery. It was thinned out"
22027,"(2027) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: About a man who gave a man money to buy and emancipate him? He said: If his master appears against him before he emancipates him, then he will get whatever he took from his price, and his slave will be taken, and if he appears Upon him, after the one who had taken him freed him, he took from the one who bought him what he had taken, so he was freed."
22028,"(22028) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He takes its price another time, and its loyalty becomes For the one who freed him."
22029,"(22029) Jarir told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no purchase for him, no emancipation for him, and whoever does that is a sinner."
22030,"(22030) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He was asked about a man who confided money to a man and he bought it. So he freed him. Al-Sha’bi said: If I had taken him, I would have punished him severely."
22031,"(22031) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hikam: Concerning a servant who went to a man and gave him money, and said: Buy me. So he bought him and freed him, then he was informed of that and said: The sale is permissible, and the price for which the slave was purchased will be taken."
22032,"(22032) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, Salim, al-Qasim, and Ata: Concerning a servant who gave to a man. He bought it and freed it. They said: It is not permissible."
22033,"(22033) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is not permissible, and whoever He did it."
22034,"(22034) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: It is not permissible, and whoever does that, is immoral"
22035,"(22035) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It reached Omar ibn al-Khattab that so-and-so He sells wine and says: What is the matter with him? The one who killed him did not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God’s curse be upon him. The Jews were forbidden from fat, so they collected it, sold it, and ate its price. (Bukhari 2223, Muslim 1207)"
22036,"(22036) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: We had wine. An orphan of ours. When the verses on the table were revealed, we asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: May God strengthen him."
22037,"(22037) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When the verse about usury was revealed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose on the pulpit and recited them to the people, then forbade trading in Wine (Bukhari 2084, Muslim 69)"
22038,"(22038) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, in a similar way. (Muslim 1206. Ahmad 6/46)"
22039,"(22039) Ibn Idris and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Tu’ma ibn Amr, on the authority of Umar ibn Bayan al-Taghlabi, on the authority of Urwah ibn Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever sells alcohol, let him pay the fine. Pigs
(Ahmad 4/253, Darmi 2102)"
22040,"(22040) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muti’ bin Abdullah, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi speaking, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: Omar said: May God curse so-and-so, because he was the first to give permission for the sale of alcohol, and trade is not suitable for things that are not permissible to eat or drink."
22041,"(22041) Ali bin Musir told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Furat, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: I was Under the pulpit of Hudhayf while he was in the cities, he thanked God and praised him, then said: As for what follows, the wine seller And those who drink them are alike in sin. Indeed, he who keeps pigs and who eats them are alike in sin."
22042,"(22042) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Shubayl, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, He said: It was reported to Omar ibn al-Khattab that a man had become wealthy by selling wine, so he said: Break all his vessels, and drive all his livestock. No"
22043,"(22043) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Wabara ibn Abd al-Rahman, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: No. It is permissible to sell alcohol, but not to drink it."
22044,"(22044) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: When alcohol was prohibited, they came to the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. They said: O Messenger of God, shall we sell it and benefit from its price? He said: Throw it away."
